t":"Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture"},"2":{"id":"/docs/architecture-0","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#why-object-capture-instead-of-wes-bos-room-pipeline","content":"Why Object Capture instead of Wes Bos' room pipeline"},"3":{"id":"/docs/architecture-1","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#contracts","content":"Contracts"},"4":{"id":"/docs/architecture-2","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"`bike-capture/1` (iOS export zip)"},"5":{"id":"/docs/architecture-3","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"Capture cache (browser storage)"},"6":{"id":"/docs/architecture-4","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"USDZ loading (`apps/web/src/viewer/usd/`)"},"7":{"id":"/docs/architecture-5","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"Rendering and performance (`apps/web/src/viewer/`)"},"8":{"id":"/docs/architecture-6","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"`bike-scene/1` (viewer JSON, `*.bike.json`)"},"9":{"id":"/docs/architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"`bike-share/1` (share package, `*.bikeshare.zip`) and the customer link"},"10":{"id":"/docs/architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"Photo close-ups"},"11":{"id":"/docs/architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"Open questions (verify on device)"},"12":{"id":"/docs/architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#why-object-capture-instead-of-wes-bos-room-pipeline","content":"`wesbos/3d-model-anything` records RoomPlan + LiDAR mesh + posed photos, then an AI agent\nrebuilds the room in three.js. A bike is one object with thin tubes, spokes and cables, so we\nuse Apple's Object Capture: guided orbits, **automatic object masking** (the background is\nremoved during reconstruction; no green screen needed) and a textured USDZ. We keep Wes's\nkey idea of **posed photos**: `poses.json` tells us where each photo was taken, so the viewer\ncan show real close-up photos for an area (e.g. the fork crown) next to the 3D view."},"13":{"id":"/docs/architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#why-object-capture-instead-of-wes-bos-room-pipeline","content":"Fallbacks when Object Capture struggles with a bike (thin spokes are the classic failure):\narea mode + a crop box, or a gaussian splat (Scaniverse/Polycam/Luma) for photoreal paint.\nThe green background mode exists for compositing snapshots/videos in other tools."},"14":{"id":"/docs/architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"| Path            | Content                                                                                                                 |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `manifest.json` | `{ schema, name, createdAt, device, systemVersion, mode: \"object\"\\|\"area\", model, poses, images, photos?, imageCount }` |","table":"table-0"},"15":{"id":"/docs/architecture-13","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"| Path         | Content                       |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| `model.usdz` | reconstruction, meters, +Y up |","table":"table-0"},"16":{"id":"/docs/architecture-14","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"| Path         | Content                                                                                              |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `poses.json` | `{ schema: \"bike-poses/1\", samples: [{ sample, file, transform[16] }] }` (column-major camera→model) |","table":"table-0"},"17":{"id":"/docs/architecture-15","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"| Path      | Content                                           |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `images/` | Object Capture HEIC photos (reconstruction input) |","table":"table-0"},"18":{"id":"/docs/architecture-16","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"| Path      | Content                                                                                                                                                       |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `photos/` | optional: JPEG copies of `images/`, same file stems, ≤ 2048 px long edge, EXIF orientation baked into the pixels (orientation 1). Listed as `manifest.photos` |","table":"table-0"},"19":{"id":"/docs/architecture-17","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"| Path          | Content             |\n| ------------- | ------------------- |\n| `record.json` | app-internal record |","table":"table-0"},"20":{"id":"/docs/architecture-18","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"Importing in the browser (`apps/web/src/scene/capture.ts`): dropping a `*.bikecapture.zip`\nunzips it in memory with fflate; nothing is uploaded. The iOS exporter zips its staging folder\n(`NSFileCoordinator .forUploading`), so files usually sit under one top-level directory: the\nshallowest `manifest.json` defines the bundle root and `__MACOSX/` / `._*` entries are ignored.\nOnly `manifest.json`, the model and `poses.json` are decompressed (size-capped); images are just\nlisted; when `manifest.photos` names a non-empty folder, its JPEGs are used instead of the HEICs\n(pose `file` names like `IMG_0007.HEIC` match `IMG_0007.jpg` by stem), so no browser needs the\nWASM HEIC decoder. If `manifest.model` is missing, a `glb`/`gltf`/`usdz`/`ply` next to the manifest is used\n(GLB first, e.g. after `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`). A broken `poses.json` is a warning, not an error."},"21":{"id":"/docs/architecture-19","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"The resulting scene gets a stable id (`capture-<name>-<createdAt digits>`) so dropping the same\nbundle again restores its saved areas and comments, and a model URL `bundle:<zip name>/<path>`,\nwhich is never fetched: it is resolved from memory or from the capture cache below, and only\nwhen neither has it does the viewer ask for that zip to be dropped again."},"22":{"id":"/docs/architecture-20","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"So a capture scene survives a reload, every successfully opened bundle is kept in the browser\n(`apps/web/src/scene/captureCache.ts`, pure logic; `apps/web/src/storage/backends.ts`, storage):"},"23":{"id":"/docs/architecture-21","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**What**: the model bytes, `manifest.json`, `poses.json` and the image list. Lazily extracted\nfiles (photos, thumbnails) can be added to an entry later (`putFile`) and are evicted with it.\nThe zip itself is not kept (HEIC photos make it hundreds of MB)."},"24":{"id":"/docs/architecture-22","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**Where**: OPFS (`navigator.storage.getDirectory()`, folder `bike-captures/`, flat\npercent-encoded file names), falling back to IndexedDB (`bike-3d-brew` / `files`) when OPFS is\nmissing, has no `createWritable()` (older Safari) or refuses a probe write. Neither → no cache,\nthe old \"drop the zip again\" behavior. `navigator.storage.persist()` is requested once per page\nload, on the first store."},"25":{"id":"/docs/architecture-23","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**Keys**: one entry per `bundle:` model URL; files live under `cap-<slug>-<fnv1a(url)>/…` and an\n`index.json` lists entries (validated on read). An entry remembers the scene id it was opened\nas, so a different bike exported with the same zip filename never loads the wrong model."},"26":{"id":"/docs/architecture-24","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**Budget**: LRU by last use, `min(500 MB, 50% of the quota − other usage)` from\n`navigator.storage.estimate()`. A bundle larger than the whole budget is simply not cached."},"27":{"id":"/docs/architecture-25","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**Failure**: every call is best effort. Any storage error leaves the app as if the cache did\nnot exist; entries whose files vanished (browser eviction) are dropped from the index."},"28":{"id":"/docs/architecture-26","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**UI**: \"Open…\" becomes a small menu once something is stored: \"Choose a file…\" plus the stored\ncaptures (name, size, × to forget)."},"29":{"id":"/docs/architecture-27","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"Object Capture writes a USDZ whose root layer is **binary USDC (crate)**: one baked triangle\nmesh, indexed face-varying `primvars:st` and normals, a `UsdPreviewSurface` fed by\n`UsdUVTexture` PNGs in `0/` (diffuse, normal with scale 2 / bias -1, occlusion),\n`metersPerUnit = 1`, `upAxis = \"Y\"`."},"30":{"id":"/docs/architecture-28","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"three.js r186 can read this: `USDLoader` (the old `USDZLoader` is a deprecated alias) has a crate\nparser with LZ4 + integer decoding (`usd/USDCParser.js`) and a composer that handles xforms,\nGeomSubsets, indexed/face-varying primvars, UsdPreviewSurface textures, `metersPerUnit` and Z-up.\nWe reuse those parsers and patch what fails on real-world files:"},"31":{"id":"/docs/architecture-29","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"`crate.ts` (`CrateParser`): values the crate stores **inline** that r186 misreads: small integral\n`double2/3/4` and `half3/4` (packed int8, e.g. `xformOp:translate = (0, 0, 5)` became a number and\ncrashed the transform), negative `int`, `half`; plus scalar `half3/4`, `quath`, `int4`, `matrix2d/3d`."},"32":{"id":"/docs/architecture-30","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"`composer.ts` (`FastUSDComposer`): typed-array fast path for all-triangle meshes. Stock three took\n~1.4–2.2 s to build a 1M-triangle mesh (JS arrays per index); this takes ~0.2 s, same output."},"33":{"id":"/docs/architecture-31","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"`usdz.ts` (`loadUsd`): unzips only USD layers and images, takes the first layer as root (falls back\nto the first USD layer anywhere), composes, welds the face-varying expansion back into an indexed\nmesh (`../weld.ts`: 2.9M → 0.49M vertices for 1M triangles), waits for textures (blob URLs created and revoked by\nthree per image), halves three's normal-map strength for the standard scale 2 / bias -1 decode,\nand reports undecodable textures as warnings instead of failing."},"34":{"id":"/docs/architecture-32","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"Measured on a synthetic 23 MB USDZ (972k triangles, 2048² texture; `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py\n--detail 90 --tex 2048`), Chromium: unzip 16 ms, parse 183 ms, build 206 ms, textures 24 ms. Parsing\nstays on the main thread: a worker would save the ~0.2 s parse but pay ~0.07 s structured-clone of\nthe spec table back, and the build step needs three.js objects on the main thread anyway. The USD\ncode (~70 KB min) is a lazy chunk loaded on the first USDZ. Anything that still fails shows an error\npointing to `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`. Fixtures are synthetic (`apps/web/test/fixtures/README.md`)."},"35":{"id":"/docs/architecture-33","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"Details and measurements: PERFORMANCE.md."},"36":{"id":"/docs/architecture-34","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"**Render on demand** (`renderScheduler.ts`): the animation loop only runs while something changes.\nViewer methods (`setModel`, `setView`, `applyTransform`, `setBackground`, resize, controls input,\nfly-to) call `viewer.requestRender()`; **code that mutates the three.js scene directly must call it\ntoo**. The shadow map is redrawn only on `requestRender()` (scene changes), never for camera-only\nframes. Frame listeners (`onFrame`, pins) run after drawn frames only."},"37":{"id":"/docs/architecture-35","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"**Quality** (`quality.ts`): pixel ratio ≤ 2 (1.5 on phones for captures over 400k triangles),\nMSAA only at 1×, smaller hard shadows on phones; `?quality=low|high` overrides."},"38":{"id":"/docs/architecture-36","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"**Raycasts** (`bvh.ts`): after the first frame of a model, meshes over 5k triangles get a\nthree-mesh-bvh hierarchy (built in `bvh.worker.ts` for big meshes, indirect so the GPU index buffer\nis untouched). `viewer.raycastReady` tells the pins when occlusion tests are cheap."},"39":{"id":"/docs/architecture-37","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"**Pins** (`pins.ts`): allocation-free projection against a cached viewport size, transform-only\nwrites for pins that moved, `offscreen` class for pins behind the camera or off the stage,\nocclusion raycasts under a 3 ms per-frame budget that finish on idle animation frames."},"40":{"id":"/docs/architecture-38","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"**GLB decoders** (`loaders.ts`, `gltfInfo.ts`): `extensionsUsed` decides which of Meshopt, Draco\nand KTX2/Basis is imported; their WASM ships in the build (no CDN)."},"41":{"id":"/docs/architecture-39","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"See `apps/web/src/scene/schema.ts`. A scene references its model by URL (relative to the\nscene file), lists **hotspots** (named camera views: the zoomable areas) and **annotations**\n(surface point + normal, title, body, kind `feature|spec|upgrade|note`, optional price and area).\nAll coordinates are in model-root space."},"42":{"id":"/docs/architecture-40","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"**Model transform.** The loader wraps the model so its native bounding box is centered on X/Z\nand rests on y = 0 (`centerOnGround`, deterministic per file); that frame is *model-root space*.\n`model.scale`, `model.rotation` (Euler XYZ, three.js convention) and `model.offset` are then\napplied to the root as `world = offset + R · (scale · p)`. Annotations and hotspot views stay in\nmodel-root space, so re-orienting a capture never detaches a comment. The overview camera is\nframed in world space (camera up is world +Y) and converted back."},"43":{"id":"/docs/architecture-41","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"**Crop box** (`crop?: { min, max, enabled }`, model-root space, optional and lenient: a\nmalformed crop is dropped, swapped corners are reordered). The viewer turns it into six world\nclipping planes on the model's own materials (local clipping, shadows clipped too), recomputed only\nwhen the model transform or the box changes. Raycasts skip hits outside the box (no comments on\ncropped-away parts, no occlusion by them), pins outside it are hidden, and exact bounds (framing,\non-ground, auto-orient samples) only count kept vertices. Edit mode shows the box with one handle\nper face (`viewer/cropBox.ts`): pointer events in the capture phase, so mouse and touch drags never\norbit the camera; the face moves along its axis to the point nearest the pointer ray, clipping\nlive, and the store is updated once on release. \"Fit to bike\" (`scene/crop.ts`, pure) samples\npoints along triangle edges, cuts above the floor slab (a dense, wide band in the lower third of\nthe up axis) and keeps the largest 26-connected voxel cluster with a 2% margin. Area-mode captures\nget that box pre-computed but disabled, a hint in the toast, and auto-orient waits until the crop\nis on. Turning the crop on/off or fitting it re-grounds the visible part."},"44":{"id":"/docs/architecture-42","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"**Auto-orient** (`apps/web/src/scene/orient.ts`, pure, unit-tested). Target frame: +X front,\n+Y up, +Z drive side, tyres on y = 0. Up to 50k strided vertices (≈3 ms for 1M vertices):"},"45":{"id":"/docs/architecture-43","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"PCA: smallest-variance axis = the bike's width, middle axis = candidate up."},"46":{"id":"/docs/architecture-44","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"Up sign by votes: the centroid sits below mid-height (wheels), and the top band (handlebar) is\nwider across than the bottom band (two tyre contact patches)."},"47":{"id":"/docs/architecture-45","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"Ground line: the longest downward-facing edge of the side-view convex hull (tangent across\nboth tyres) fixes the 5–15° tilt PCA leaves."},"48":{"id":"/docs/architecture-46","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"Object Capture output is gravity-aligned, so if that up is within 6° of ±Y, Y is kept exactly\nand only yaw changes (horizontal PCA)."},"49":{"id":"/docs/architecture-47","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"Front sign: the wide handlebar sits ahead of centre (plus a small vote for the drivetrain mass\nbehind it). Drive side follows from the right-handed frame."},"50":{"id":"/docs/architecture-48","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"It runs once when a scene is opened with a non-demo model, no comments and no `model.rotation`\n(`shouldAutoOrient`); the offset is then recomputed from exact bounds so the bike stands on the\nground. Edit → Model exposes the result plus manual rotate/flip/scale/nudge, each one store\nupdate with a small undo stack. Generate tilted test bundles with\n`node tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs --rotate 70,25,-40` (ASCII USD mesh in `model.usdz`)."},"51":{"id":"/docs/architecture-49","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"Share → \"Export share package\" turns a local capture into a self-contained zip\n(`apps/web/src/scene/share.ts`):"},"52":{"id":"/docs/architecture-50","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"| Path              | Content                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike-share.json` | `{ schema: \"bike-share/1\", id, name, createdAt, scene, model, photos }` |","table":"table-1"},"53":{"id":"/docs/architecture-51","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"| Path              | Content                                                            |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `scene.bike.json` | the `bike-scene/1` scene, model URL rewritten to the packaged file |","table":"table-1"},"54":{"id":"/docs/architecture-52","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"| Path                 | Content      |\n| -------------------- | ------------ |\n| `model.glb\\|usdz\\|…` | the 3D model |","table":"table-1"},"55":{"id":"/docs/architecture-53","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"| Path           | Content                                      |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `photos/*.jpg` | the close-ups referenced by `Hotspot.photos` |","table":"table-1"},"56":{"id":"/docs/architecture-54","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"`tools/publish-scene.mjs` validates a package (size limits: zip 300 MB, model 250 MB, JSON 2 MB,\n8 MB × 64 photos; JPEG only; no paths outside the package; `parseScene`) and installs it under\n`apps/web/public/scenes/<id>/`. The customer link is\n`…/app/?scene=scenes/<id>/scene.bike.json&view=present` (`kiosk=1&interval=<s>&idle=<s>` for a\nshop screen). Scene, model and photo URLs must be same-origin or https."},"57":{"id":"/docs/architecture-55","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"`src/entry.ts` loads only `present/BikePresenter.ts` for `?view=present`, so customers never\ndownload editing code. The presenter is a self-contained module: `mountPresenter(container,\noptions)` returns a controller with `goToArea`, `next`, `prev`, `play`, `pause`, `setBackground`\nand `on(event)` for `ready`, `error`, `areachange` and `commentopen`. It scopes its CSS under\n`.bike-present` and only takes keys while focused, which is the base for an iframe embed or a\n`<bike-viewer>` element (see ROADMAP)."},"58":{"id":"/docs/architecture-56","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"For the active area (its view target, preferring cameras on the side its saved view looks from),\nthe active comment (its pin, preferring cameras in front of its surface normal) and each Present\nstep, the viewer shows a filmstrip of the capture photos that best show that point; tapping one\nopens a full-screen viewer (arrows / swipe, pinch / wheel / double-tap zoom, Esc)."},"59":{"id":"/docs/architecture-57","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"**Spaces.** A pose is a column-major camera→reconstruction matrix, camera looking down -Z,\n+Y up. Scene positions are in model-root space. `Viewer.setModel` adds `centerOnGround(object)`\nto the model root, so `modelRoot ⟵ reconstruction` is the loaded object's local matrix (the\ncentering shift plus any root transform the loader applied) times the identity wrapper:\n`src/viewer/captureSpace.ts`. The scene's `model.rotation/scale/offset` sit on the model root\nitself and never enter the mapping. A unit test runs the fixture USDZ through three's\n`USDLoader` + `centerOnGround` and checks the expected close-ups win."},"60":{"id":"/docs/architecture-58","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"**Ranking** (`src/scene/photos.ts`, pure): keep photos whose frustum contains the target\n(assumed iPhone wide camera, 65° × 51°, landscape sensor; poses carry no intrinsics), drop\ncameras behind the surface (`side` hint), score `0.45·centered + 0.35·closeness + 0.2·facing`\n(closeness relative to the nearest usable photo, so units do not matter), and skip near-duplicate\nviewpoints. Occlusion is not tested."},"61":{"id":"/docs/architecture-59","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"**Photos** (`src/ui/photoLibrary.ts`): extracted one at a time from the dropped zip via its\ncentral directory (`src/scene/zipIndex.ts`: the `File` stays on disk, nothing else is inflated),\ndecoded natively (`createImageBitmap`, then `<img>`; Safari reads HEIC), else HEIC goes to a\nmodule worker that lazily loads libheif (`libheif-js`, WASM, ~2 MB, LGPL-3.0, only fetched when a\nHEIC photo is shown). Results are downscaled to JPEG (360 px thumbnails, 2048 px full) and added\nto the capture cache entry, so after a reload the photos already seen still show without the zip."},"62":{"id":"/docs/architecture-60","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"Does `PhotogrammetrySession.Poses` return camera→model transforms in the same frame as the\nUSDZ? (Assumed, and the photo close-ups depend on it; validate by checking that an area's top\nclose-up really shows that area on a real capture.)"},"63":{"id":"/docs/architecture-61","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"~~Does three.js read Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC)?~~ Yes, with the fixes above, verified on\nsynthetic Object-Capture-like files. Still to confirm on a real capture (docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md)."},"64":{"id":"/docs/architecture-62","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"Bike size vs. Object Capture's bounding box limits: area mode is the fallback."},"65":{"id":"/docs/architecture-63","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"_Source: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`_"},"66":{"id":"/docs/changelog","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"page","content":"Changelog","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Plan"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog"},"67":{"id":"/docs/changelog-0","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"Unreleased"},"68":{"id":"/docs/changelog-1","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Added"},"69":{"id":"/docs/changelog-2","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#fixed","content":"Fixed"},"70":{"id":"/docs/changelog-3","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog","content":"Every PR adds a line under **Unreleased** (newest first) with its PR number. When the owner\nmerges the stack to `main`, the Unreleased block becomes a dated release."},"71":{"id":"/docs/changelog-4","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Site follows the stack tip: `pages.yml` republishes whenever the newest ready PR at the top of the stack (or `develop` when none is open) is pushed, so the live site no longer waits for merges. Parallel agents work in `.claude/worktrees/` with their own E2E port; the suite no longer reuses a server it did not start. The session-credits counter is gone from the home page. (#17)"},"72":{"id":"/docs/changelog-5","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"iOS capture guidance + JPEG photos: the capture screen has a checklist (3 orbits at hub height, saddle height and top-down, ticked as Object Capture completes each pass; close-ups of fork crown, dropouts, rear derailleur and cockpit; shots per pass; reflective-paint tips, and why a turntable does not work with on-device Object Capture). Exported bundles add `photos/*.jpg` (2048 px, upright) listed as `manifest.photos`, and the web viewer uses them instead of decoding HEIC. (#14)"},"73":{"id":"/docs/changelog-6","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"WebKit E2E: the iPhone specs also run in Playwright WebKit (Safari's engine) via `npm run e2e:webkit` (local, on a Mac; CI is a roadmap item). (#16)"},"74":{"id":"/docs/changelog-7","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Auto-publish: every push to `develop` republishes the site (`.github/workflows/pages.yml`), and each open PR from this repo gets a preview at `/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (docs + viewer), removed when the PR closes (`pr-preview.yml`), listed under \"PR previews\" on the home and Progress pages from `/pr/index.json`. `tools/publish-pages.sh` gains `--pr`, `--title` and `--remove-pr`, only replaces its own part of gh-pages (the main site keeps `/pr/`), and retries on the latest gh-pages when another run pushed first. (#15)"},"75":{"id":"/docs/changelog-8","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Performance: the viewer renders on demand (an idle stage draws 0 frames, the loop pauses in hidden tabs), redraws the shadow map only when the scene changes, caps the pixel ratio per device (`?quality=low|high`), welds USDZ meshes into indexed geometry (2.9M → 0.49M vertices on a 1M-triangle capture), builds a BVH in a worker so picking and pin occlusion cost ~0.05 ms instead of ~200 ms, and updates 50+ pins with budgeted occlusion and transform-only writes. GLBs with Meshopt, Draco or KTX2 load with lazily fetched, self-hosted decoders; `tools/optimize-glb.mjs` makes phone-friendly GLBs; `tools/bench/bench.mjs` measures it all. See `docs/PERFORMANCE.md`. (#12)"},"76":{"id":"/docs/changelog-9","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Photos & video → 3D research (`docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md`): reconstruction options for bikes, recommendation (Object Capture on macOS by default, COLMAP + OpenMVS as fallback, splats later), photo and video capture protocols, owner decisions; new ROADMAP Milestone 1.5. (#11)"},"77":{"id":"/docs/changelog-10","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Share with customers: read-only `?scene=…&view=present` link served by a standalone presenter (`present/BikePresenter.ts`, no editing code, container-scoped), Share button (share sheet / clipboard / visible link), `bike-share/1` package export + `tools/publish-scene.mjs`, published demo at `scenes/demo/`. Present mode: leader lines, progress dots, swipe, auto-play (`?kiosk=1`), phone bottom sheet; markdown-lite comment bodies (DOM-only renderer); drag / ↑↓ comment reordering. (#8)"},"78":{"id":"/docs/changelog-11","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Crop box: Edit → Model → Crop clips everything outside an axis-aligned box (model-root space, saved as optional `crop` in `bike-scene/1`) with renderer clipping planes; drag the face handles (mouse or touch) or type the corners; \"Fit to bike\" removes the floor slab and background clusters. Cropped-away geometry can't take comments, and comments outside the box are hidden. Area-mode captures get a suggested box and a hint. (#10)"},"79":{"id":"/docs/changelog-12","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Auto-orient captures: a scanned bike is stood upright facing +X (PCA + side-view ground line, bike-shaped sign heuristics) on first load, with a toast; Edit → Model has Auto-orient, rotate ±90° per axis, flip, turn 180°, scale, real length in cm, 1 cm nudges, on-ground, undo and reset. Comments stay attached. `tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs` generates tilted test bundles. (#9)"},"80":{"id":"/docs/changelog-13","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Test system: Playwright E2E suite (`npm run e2e`, desktop + iPhone viewport, sharded CI job) over the production build, covering every viewer flow including stored captures, photo close-ups and binary USDC; synthetic capture-bundle fixtures (`tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`, rendered-photo bundle via `render-photos.mjs`); unit coverage with ratcheting thresholds (`npm run test:coverage`, ~99.8% lines) incl. zip64 parsing, OPFS/IndexedDB backends and the photo UI; `docs/TESTING.md`. UI decisions moved into tested `scene/helpers.ts`; `?e2e` test hook. Fixed: a tap right after an instant (reduced-motion) fly-to missed the model. (#7)"},"81":{"id":"/docs/changelog-14","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Photo close-ups: for the active area, the active comment and each Present step, a filmstrip of the capture photos that best show it (ranked from `poses.json`), with a full-screen viewer (swipe, arrows, pinch/zoom). Photos are read lazily from the zip, HEIC is decoded natively or by a lazily loaded WASM worker, and thumbnails are kept in the capture cache. (#6)"},"82":{"id":"/docs/changelog-15","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Captures survive reloads: opened `*.bikecapture.zip` bundles are kept in browser storage (OPFS, IndexedDB fallback, LRU under a quota-aware budget) and reopen automatically; \"Open…\" lists stored captures with size and a forget button. Synthetic fixture generator in `tools/fixtures/`. (#5)"},"83":{"id":"/docs/changelog-16","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Docs & progress site (Fumadocs, `apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown: home dashboard with roadmap progress per milestone, latest changes and build commit; \"How to test\" guide; offline search. `tools/publish-pages.sh` publishes it with the viewer (under `/app/`) and a synthetic test bundle to the `gh-pages` branch; `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` writes a synthetic `*.bikecapture.zip`. The Actions-based `pages.yml` deploy is removed. (#4)"},"84":{"id":"/docs/changelog-17","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"USDZ robustness: Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC) loads with textures; fixes three.js r186 crate decoding of inline vectors/halves/negative ints, ~10× faster mesh build for large captures, lazy-loaded USD code, clear fallback to `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`. Synthetic fixture generator `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`. (#3)"},"85":{"id":"/docs/changelog-18","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Capture bundle import: drop an iPhone `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer; it is unzipped in the browser, the model loads and the scene is named from the manifest. Re-dropping a bundle restores its comments. (#2)"},"86":{"id":"/docs/changelog-19","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Foundation: three.js viewer/editor with areas, pinned sales comments, present mode, background modes, `bike-scene/1` format; iOS Object Capture app skeleton; CI. (#1)"},"87":{"id":"/docs/changelog-20","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#fixed","content":"Customer link and Present mode in Safari: the card-height update no longer triggers a \"ResizeObserver loop\" page error. (#16)"},"88":{"id":"/docs/changelog-21","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#fixed","content":"The active comment pin (and the draft pin) drifted away from its point by 25% of its screen position because CSS `scale` also scaled the position transform. (#9)"},"89":{"id":"/docs/changelog-22","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#fixed","content":"_Source: `CHANGELOG.md`_"},"90":{"id":"/docs/goals","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"page","content":"Goals","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Plan"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals"},"91":{"id":"/docs/goals-0","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals#product","content":"Product"},"92":{"id":"/docs/goals-1","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"Success criteria"},"93":{"id":"/docs/goals-2","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"Quality bar for every PR"},"94":{"id":"/docs/goals-3","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals#non-goals-for-now","content":"Non-goals (for now)"},"95":{"id":"/docs/goals-4","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#product","content":"A bike shop captures a bike with an iPhone in a few minutes and gets a background-free,\nphotoreal 3D model that sales staff (in store, on a tablet) and customers (on a shared link)\ncan spin, zoom into named areas (fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and read pinned sales comments."},"96":{"id":"/docs/goals-5","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Capture → viewer in under 15 minutes** with no desktop software: capture on iPhone,\nAirDrop the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer."},"97":{"id":"/docs/goals-6","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Looks like the real bike**: textures, thin parts (spokes, cables) acceptable; background gone."},"98":{"id":"/docs/goals-7","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Fast on phones**: first model visible in < 3 s on iPhone Safari over 4G for a 20 MB model;\n60 fps orbiting with 50 pins."},"99":{"id":"/docs/goals-8","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Selling tool, not a 3D toy**: areas and comments are the primary UI; present mode is\nusable by a non-technical salesperson with one hand."},"100":{"id":"/docs/goals-9","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Robust**: untrusted files never crash the app; every failure says what to do next."},"101":{"id":"/docs/goals-10","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"Pure logic in `apps/web/src/scene/` with unit tests; coverage does not go down."},"102":{"id":"/docs/goals-11","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"`npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build` and the E2E suite pass; CI green."},"103":{"id":"/docs/goals-12","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"UI changes verified in Chromium with screenshots, at desktop and phone sizes."},"104":{"id":"/docs/goals-13","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"Docs (ROADMAP, CHANGELOG, ARCHITECTURE, guides) updated in the same PR."},"105":{"id":"/docs/goals-14","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#non-goals-for-now","content":"Public release / app store distribution (the owner decides when)."},"106":{"id":"/docs/goals-15","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#non-goals-for-now","content":"Real customer captures in the repo: only generated fixtures."},"107":{"id":"/docs/goals-16","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#non-goals-for-now","content":"_Source: `docs/GOALS.md`_"},"108":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"109":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Capture bikes with an iPhone, show them as background-free 3D models, zoom into components\n(fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and pin sales comments on them."},"110":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"**`apps/ios`**: iPhone capture app (Apple Object Capture: background removed automatically, on-device 3D build, camera poses, shareable bundle)."},"111":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"**`apps/web`**: three.js viewer and editor: clear / chroma-green / studio backgrounds, fly-to areas, comment pins, presentation mode, JSON export."},"112":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Drop a `.bikecapture.zip` from the iPhone app (or a `.glb`, `.usdz`, `.ply`) onto the viewer to use your own capture. Switch to **Edit** to\ntap the bike and add comments, save camera views as areas; **Present** steps through areas for\na customer."},"113":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, ROADMAP.md and\napps/ios/README.md. Inspired by\nwesbos/3d-model-anything."},"114":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"_Source: `README.md`_"},"115":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","type":"page","content":"Manual steps","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/manual-steps"},"116":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-0","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"Photos & video → 3D"},"117":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-1","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"Things an agent cannot do (hardware, accounts, decisions). Newest first."},"118":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-2","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Customer link on a real phone**: open the published demo link\n(`…/app/?scene=scenes/demo/scene.bike.json&view=present`) on an iPhone, check swiping, the\nbottom sheet, pin taps and the share sheet. Real customer captures should be published to a\nhost you control with `node tools/publish-scene.mjs <zip> --out <folder>`, not committed here."},"119":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-3","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Crop on a real area-mode capture**: capture a bike in area mode, open the bundle, turn on\nEdit → Model → Crop and check \"Fit to bike\" removes the floor and the room. Note scans where the\nbike touches a wall or stand (the box then includes it; drag the faces to fix)."},"120":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-4","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Auto-orient on a real capture** (needs the real-capture test below): open a real `.bikecapture.zip`\nand check the bike stands upright, front to the right (+X), drive side towards the default camera.\nIf not, note which button fixed it (Flip / Turn 180° / rotate) so the heuristics can be tuned."},"121":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-5","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Decide on the HEIC decoder license**: photo close-ups decode HEIC in Chrome/Firefox with\n`libheif-js` (LGPL-3.0), shipped as a separate, lazily loaded worker chunk. Fine for a private\ntool; before a public release, either confirm LGPL compliance (unmodified library in its own\nfile, notice in the about/credits) or remove it once the iOS app exports JPEGs (see ROADMAP)."},"122":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-6","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Close-ups on a real capture**: open a real `.bikecapture.zip` with a few areas and check that\neach area's first photos really show it, in Chrome (WASM HEIC path) and iPhone Safari (native)."},"123":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-7","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Real Object Capture USDZ in the viewer** (needs a real capture): drop the `model.usdz` (or\nthe `.bikecapture.zip`) on the viewer and compare with Quick Look on the Mac/iPhone: textures\npresent and not flipped, size in meters, bike upright, normal-map bumps not exaggerated. The\nbrowser console logs `USDZ …: N triangles, unzip/parse/build ms`; note those numbers in the\nPR. If anything is off, describe the file structure (`usdcat model.usdz | head -80` without\nsharing the capture) so an agent can re-create it in `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`."},"124":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-8","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Real iPhone capture test** (needs an iPhone with LiDAR, iOS 18+): build `apps/ios`, capture a\nbike, export the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer. Report whether the USDZ loads."},"125":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-9","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Capture guidance + JPEG export on a device** (#14, needs an iPhone with LiDAR): during a capture,\nopen the checklist: each completed orbit ticks the next orbit row and its shot count stays\nfixed after **Another pass**; the top bar counts shots for the current pass only. Export a\nbundle and check (a) export of ~150 photos finishes in reasonable time with the spinner, (b)\n`photos/IMG_*.jpg` are 2048 px on the long edge and **upright** for portrait and landscape\nshots (open a few on the Mac), (c) the zip grew by roughly 0.5 MB per photo, (d) close-ups in\ndesktop Chrome load without the `heic` worker. Note: the iOS app was compile-checked by CI only\n(no Xcode on the agent's Mac); the JPEG writer was verified with ImageIO on macOS."},"126":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-10","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**GitHub Pages**: done by the owner on 2026-10-27 (Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch\n`gh-pages`). The site is published from this repo by `tools/publish-pages.sh`."},"127":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-11","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Let Actions publish the site** (auto-publish on `develop` and PR previews): Settings →\nActions → General → Workflow permissions → **Read and write permissions**, so the\n`GITHUB_TOKEN` of `pages.yml` and `pr-preview.yml` may push to `gh-pages`. If `gh-pages` has a\nbranch protection rule, allow GitHub Actions to push to it. Check after the first run: the\n\"Publish site\" / \"PR preview\" run is green and Settings → Pages shows a new deployment. PRs\nonly get a preview once their branch contains `pr-preview.yml` (it runs from the PR's own\ncode), so PRs below this one in the stack get theirs after they are rebased or merged."},"128":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-12","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"Owner decisions for turning any photo set or video into a model (details in RECONSTRUCTION.md):"},"129":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-13","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"**Mac for the default path**: is an Apple silicon Mac (macOS 14+) available to run Object Capture\n(`PhotogrammetrySession`) on photo folders? Without one, the fallback is COLMAP + OpenMVS on Linux."},"130":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-14","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"**GPU box**: rent (per-hour cloud GPU) or own an NVIDIA machine for COLMAP dense and Gaussian splats? Budget?"},"131":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-15","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"**Cloud API**: use a paid service (KIRI Engine API, Luma, Polycam…)? Which one, monthly budget,\nand are its data terms acceptable for customer bikes? Needs an account and an API key stored as a secret, never in the repo."},"132":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-16","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"**Dulling spray**: acceptable on customer bikes, or only polarizer + diffuse light?"},"133":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-17","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"**Test capture**: shoot one bike with the photo protocol and one 4K video with the video protocol,\nso the pipeline can be measured on real input (keep the files out of the repo)."},"134":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-18","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"_Source: `docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md`_"},"135":{"id":"/docs/performance","page_id":"/docs/performance","type":"page","content":"Performance","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/performance"},"136":{"id":"/docs/performance-0","page_id":"/docs/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"What the viewer does"},"137":{"id":"/docs/performance-1","page_id":"/docs/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/performance#optimizing-a-capture","content":"Optimizing a capture"},"138":{"id":"/docs/performance-2","page_id":"/docs/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/performance#measuring","content":"Measuring"},"139":{"id":"/docs/performance-3","page_id":"/docs/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"Results"},"140":{"id":"/docs/performance-4","page_id":"/docs/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/performance#known-gaps","content":"Known gaps"},"141":{"id":"/docs/performance-5","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance","content":"Targets (from GOALS.md): first model visible in **< 3 s** on iPhone Safari over 4G for a\n20 MB model, **60 fps** orbiting with **50 pins**, and **low battery use when idle**."},"142":{"id":"/docs/performance-6","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area             | What                                                                                                                                                                                                  | Where                                                 |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Render on demand | The animation loop runs only while something changes (controls input and damping, a fly-to, a model / background / pin / size change). An idle stage draws **0 frames**; a hidden tab stops the loop. | `viewer/renderScheduler.ts`, `Viewer.requestRender()` |","table":"table-0"},"143":{"id":"/docs/performance-7","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area           | What                                                                                                                                                                                         | Where                                     |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Cached shadows | The sun and the model stand still while the camera orbits, so the shadow map is redrawn only when the scene changes, not for camera frames (that pass re-draws every triangle of the model). | `Viewer` (`shadowMap.autoUpdate = false`) |","table":"table-0"},"144":{"id":"/docs/performance-8","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area                        | What                                                                                                                                                         | Where    |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------- |\n| No preserved drawing buffer | The canvas keeps its last frame while idle anyway; `screenshot()` renders right before reading. Saves a full-screen copy per frame on tile-based phone GPUs. | `Viewer` |","table":"table-0"},"145":{"id":"/docs/performance-9","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area                 | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | Where               |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------- |\n| Device-aware quality | Pixel ratio ≤ 2 (phones show no gain at 3×, which shades 2.25× the pixels), 1.5 on phones for captures over 400k triangles; MSAA only at 1× (2× already supersamples); 1024² hard shadows on phones, 2048² soft on desktop. `?quality=low` (1×, 512² shadows) and `?quality=high` (up to 3×, MSAA) override. | `viewer/quality.ts` |","table":"table-0"},"146":{"id":"/docs/performance-10","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area               | What                                                                                                                                                                                 | Where                           |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------- |\n| Welded USDZ meshes | three expands face-varying primvars to three vertices per triangle; identical corners are merged back into an indexed mesh (O(n) open-addressing hash over typed arrays, bit-exact). | `viewer/weld.ts`, `usd/usdz.ts` |","table":"table-0"},"147":{"id":"/docs/performance-11","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area         | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Where                                          |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| BVH raycasts | After the first frame of a model, meshes over 5k triangles get a three-mesh-bvh hierarchy, built in a worker for big meshes (copies, never transfers, so the geometry stays usable; indirect, so the GPU index buffer is untouched). Picking and pin occlusion use it. | `viewer/bvh.ts`, `bvhImpl.ts`, `bvh.worker.ts` |","table":"table-0"},"148":{"id":"/docs/performance-12","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | Where            |\n| ---- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| Pins | Projection into a scratch object against a cached viewport size (no layout reads), transform-only writes for pins that moved, an `offscreen` class for pins behind the camera or off the stage, occlusion raycasts under a 3 ms per-frame budget that continue on idle animation frames (without re-rendering) until every visible pin is current. Skipped until the BVH exists for big models. | `viewer/pins.ts` |","table":"table-0"},"149":{"id":"/docs/performance-13","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area                       | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | Where                                     |\n| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Lazy, self-hosted decoders | A GLB's `extensionsUsed` decides which decoder is imported: Meshopt (~26 KB JS with inline WASM), Draco (glTF build, ~190 KB WASM, workers), KTX2/Basis (~530 KB WASM, workers). three's loaders resolve the files with `new URL(…, import.meta.url)`, so Vite ships them in `dist/assets/`; nothing comes from a CDN. Plain GLBs fetch none. | `viewer/loaders.ts`, `viewer/gltfInfo.ts` |","table":"table-0"},"150":{"id":"/docs/performance-14","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"Rule for new code: anything that changes what the canvas shows outside the `Viewer` methods\n(a new scene object, a material tweak, clipping planes) must call `viewer.requestRender()`, or the\nchange appears only on the next camera move."},"151":{"id":"/docs/performance-15","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#optimizing-a-capture","content":"`tools/optimize-glb.mjs` turns a GLB (for a USDZ capture, first `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`) into a\nphone-friendly one with glTF Transform:"},"152":{"id":"/docs/performance-16","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#optimizing-a-capture","content":"**Meshopt** (default) decodes fastest and has the smallest decoder; **Draco** compresses geometry\nharder but costs a ~190 KB WASM download and slower decoding."},"153":{"id":"/docs/performance-17","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#optimizing-a-capture","content":"`--simplify <ratio>` (meshoptimizer's simplifier, `--error` as a fraction of the mesh radius,\ndefault 0.001) is the decimation step for phones: Object Capture's `.full` detail is far more than a\n6\" screen shows."},"154":{"id":"/docs/performance-18","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#optimizing-a-capture","content":"`--textures webp|--max-texture` use sharp (installed with glTF Transform). `ktx2` (ETC1S) keeps\ntextures compressed in GPU memory (a 4096² texture: 64 MB as RGBA8, 8–16 MB transcoded to ETC2, ASTC or BC7), the\nbiggest memory win on phones, and needs `toktx` on PATH."},"155":{"id":"/docs/performance-19","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#measuring","content":"The script serves `dist/` with `vite preview`, drives Chromium on SwiftShader (like the E2E suite)\nthrough the `?e2e` test hook and prints JSON: boot time, a synchronous **frame cost** (render + a\n1-pixel readback that waits for the GPU), renders while idle and while orbiting with the mouse\n(with and without 50 pins), pin-update time per frame, and for `--model`: time until the first frame\nwith the model, geometry size, JS heap, frame cost and the cost of one `pick()` / `isOccluded()`."},"156":{"id":"/docs/performance-20","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#measuring","content":"SwiftShader renders on the CPU, so absolute numbers are far from a phone GPU and swing with machine\nload: compare runs made back to back on the same machine, and read render counts and per-operation\ncosts rather than fps."},"157":{"id":"/docs/performance-21","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"Chromium + SwiftShader, 1280×800 at 1×, on a shared 4-core container under heavy load (other jobs\nrunning): treat absolute times as noisy, compare before/after. `tools/bench/bench.mjs --model big.usdz`\n(synthetic 23 MB USDZ, 972k triangles, 2048² textures), base branch vs. this change:"},"158":{"id":"/docs/performance-22","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                           | Before          | After |\n| -------------------------------- | --------------- | ----- |\n| Demo, idle stage: renders in 3 s | 8 (every frame) | **0** |","table":"table-1"},"159":{"id":"/docs/performance-23","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                                  | Before | After |\n| --------------------------------------- | ------ | ----- |\n| Demo with 50 pins, idle: renders in 3 s | 5      | **0** |","table":"table-1"},"160":{"id":"/docs/performance-24","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                                  | Before            | After               |\n| --------------------------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------- |\n| Big capture: vertices / geometry memory | 2,916,000 / 89 MB | **490,148 / 26 MB** |","table":"table-1"},"161":{"id":"/docs/performance-25","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                          | Before | After          |\n| ------------------------------- | ------ | -------------- |\n| Big capture: JS heap after load | 271 MB | **104–123 MB** |","table":"table-1"},"162":{"id":"/docs/performance-26","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                    | Before | After       |\n| ------------------------- | ------ | ----------- |\n| Big capture: one `pick()` | 179 ms | **0.07 ms** |","table":"table-1"},"163":{"id":"/docs/performance-27","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                          | Before | After       |\n| ------------------------------- | ------ | ----------- |\n| Big capture: one `isOccluded()` | 221 ms | **0.02 ms** |","table":"table-1"},"164":{"id":"/docs/performance-28","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                                      | Before | After    |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------ | -------- |\n| Big capture: pin update per frame (50 pins) | 873 ms | **2 ms** |","table":"table-1"},"165":{"id":"/docs/performance-29","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                                           | Before  | After                                          |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| Big capture: full frame cost (render + GPU sync) | 3776 ms | 2978–3038 ms (no shadow pass on camera frames) |","table":"table-1"},"166":{"id":"/docs/performance-30","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                                  | Before  | After                                                        |\n| --------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Big capture: first frame with the model | 3357 ms | 2466–4113 ms (noise; adds weld, BVH moved after first frame) |","table":"table-1"},"167":{"id":"/docs/performance-31","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"Weld cost: ~0.2 s for 3M vertices in Node on an idle core (unrolled position/normal/uv path), BVH\nbuild ~1 s, now in a worker. Real-device numbers are still to be taken (see Known gaps)."},"168":{"id":"/docs/performance-32","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#known-gaps","content":"Not yet measured on a real iPhone (ROADMAP: \"Measure on a real iPhone\")."},"169":{"id":"/docs/performance-33","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#known-gaps","content":"Parsing and welding a big USDZ still run on the main thread (~1 s together for 1M triangles on a\ndesktop CPU, more on a phone); ROADMAP \"Progressive capture loading\"."},"170":{"id":"/docs/performance-34","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#known-gaps","content":"No runtime decimation: phones get the full capture unless it went through `optimize-glb --simplify`."},"171":{"id":"/docs/performance-35","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#known-gaps","content":"The Basis transcoder path is not exercised in CI (the KTX2 fixture is uncompressed RGBA8, since Node\nhas no Basis encoder); its files are built and served like Draco's."},"172":{"id":"/docs/performance-36","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#known-gaps","content":"_Source: `docs/PERFORMANCE.md`_"},"173":{"id":"/docs/progress","page_id":"/docs/progress","type":"page","content":"Progress","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/progress"},"174":{"id":"/docs/progress-0","page_id":"/docs/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/progress","content":"Roadmap status per milestone, generated from ROADMAP.md at build time."},"175":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"page","content":"Photos & video → 3D: reconstruction options for bikes","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction"},"176":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-0","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#why-bikes-are-hard","content":"Why bikes are hard"},"177":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-1","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"Options"},"178":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-2","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#recommendation","content":"Recommendation"},"179":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-3","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"Capture protocol (photos)"},"180":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-4","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-video","content":"Capture protocol (video)"},"181":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-5","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#pipeline-planned-shape-toolsreconstruct","content":"Pipeline (planned shape: `tools/reconstruct/`)"},"182":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-6","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#owner-decisions","content":"Owner decisions"},"183":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-7","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction","content":"> \"We can have the best 3D experience, but if it doesn't come from a collection of photos and\n> videos of a bike, it's not useful.\" (owner)"},"184":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-8","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction","content":"Goal: **any photo set or video of a bike (any camera) → a `bike-capture/1` bundle the viewer\nopens**: a model (GLB preferred), `poses.json`, `images/` and `manifest.json`. Today the only\nproducer is the iOS Object Capture app."},"185":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-9","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction","content":"**Status of the facts below (2026-10-27).** This first pass comes from the author's own knowledge\nof these tools. It was **not** re-checked against vendor pages in this session because the budget\nwas cut short. Prices, limits and terms of cloud services change often: check each `verify:` item\nbefore anyone commits money or customer photos. What was checked in the sandbox: Ubuntu 24.04\nships `colmap 3.9.1` in `universe` (`apt-get install colmap` works, CPU build without CUDA). There\nis no Docker daemon and no GPU here, so OpenMVS and dense reconstruction were not run."},"186":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-10","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#why-bikes-are-hard","content":"| Property                                 | Effect on photogrammetry                                                                                                  | Mitigation                                                                                                                  |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Thin parts (spokes ~2 mm, cables, chain) | Few pixels wide, so few features. Dense MVS fills them in or drops them. Meshes come out with webbed wheels or no spokes. | Close passes at the wheels; accept \"disc\" wheels or model spokes procedurally later; splats handle them better than meshes. |","table":"table-0"},"187":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-11","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#why-bikes-are-hard","content":"| Property                        | Effect on photogrammetry                                                                       | Mitigation                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Glossy / metallic paint, chrome | Highlights move with the viewpoint, which breaks feature matching and creates holes and bumps. | Diffuse, overcast-like light (softboxes, cloudy day, shade); polarizer; dulling / 3D-scanning spray (AESUB Blue vanishes in about 4 h) on matte-safe parts only, never without the shop's OK. |","table":"table-0"},"188":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-12","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#why-bikes-are-hard","content":"| Property                  | Effect on photogrammetry      | Mitigation                                                               |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Black tyres, black carbon | Low texture, so few features. | More light; textured backdrop and floor so the camera poses still solve. |","table":"table-0"},"189":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-13","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#why-bikes-are-hard","content":"| Property                        | Effect on photogrammetry                               | Mitigation                                                                               |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Size ~1.7 × 1 m, open structure | Background visible through the frame; masking matters. | Plain backdrop or a turntable; object masking (Object Capture does it, COLMAP does not). |","table":"table-0"},"190":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-14","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#why-bikes-are-hard","content":"| Property        | Effect on photogrammetry                       | Mitigation                                                    |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Symmetric sides | Matching can confuse the left and right sides. | Overlapping rings, top-down ring, markers/props on the floor. |","table":"table-0"},"191":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-15","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"| Option                                                         | Input                                                                                   | Runs on                                                                                                     | Thin parts                     | Gloss | Output                                                                                     | Cost            | Verdict     |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------- | ----------- |\n| **Apple Object Capture** (`PhotogrammetrySession`, RealityKit) | Any folder of JPEG/HEIC/PNG (not only iPhone photos); depth and gravity help if present | macOS 12+ (detail levels `.reduced` … `.raw`; Apple silicon or a Mac with a capable GPU), iOS 17+ on device | Fair; better with close passes | Fair  | USDZ (textured), poses via `.poses` request (macOS 14 / iOS 17+), automatic object masking | Free with a Mac | **Default** |","table":"table-1"},"192":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-16","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"| Option                                                                | Input                        | Runs on                                                                                                                                             | Thin parts   | Gloss | Output                                                      | Cost                          | Verdict                              |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| **COLMAP** (SfM + MVS) + **OpenMVS** (densify, mesh, refine, texture) | Any images; video via frames | Linux/macOS/Windows; Docker; SfM fine on CPU; COLMAP dense *needs* CUDA, OpenMVS dense runs on CPU (slow: tens of minutes to hours for 150 × 12 MP) | Poor to fair | Poor  | PLY/OBJ + texture; camera poses (`cameras/images/points3D`) | Free (BSD / AGPL for OpenMVS) | **Fallback** (Linux, server, no Mac) |","table":"table-1"},"193":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-17","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"| Option                     | Input  | Runs on                                   | Thin parts   | Gloss | Output        | Cost        | Verdict                                          |\n| -------------------------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------- | ------------ | ----- | ------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Meshroom / AliceVision** | Images | Linux/Windows, CUDA needed for depth maps | Poor to fair | Poor  | OBJ + texture | Free (MPL2) | Worse than COLMAP + OpenMVS for automation; skip |","table":"table-1"},"194":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-18","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"| Option                                                                                                           | Input                                    | Runs on                                                                                    | Thin parts                               | Gloss                           | Output                                | Cost                           | Verdict                                                       |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Gaussian splatting** (nerfstudio `splatfacto`, gsplat, Postshot; apps: Polycam, Luma, Scaniverse, KIRI Engine) | Video or images, plus SfM poses (COLMAP) | NVIDIA GPU for training (minutes); phone apps do it in the cloud or on device (Scaniverse) | **Good** (looks right, not a clean mesh) | **Good** (view-dependent color) | `.ply` / `.spz` splats; no clean mesh | Free (open source) / app plans | **Photoreal option**: needs splat viewer support (ROADMAP M6) |","table":"table-1"},"195":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-19","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"| Option                                                                                                                     | Input               | Runs on                        | Thin parts | Gloss  | Output           | Cost                                                                                                                                                                                                       | Verdict                                                          |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------ | ---------- | ------ | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Cloud photogrammetry APIs**: KIRI Engine API (photo scan + 3DGS), Luma API, Polycam, RealityCapture / RealityScan (Epic) | Upload photos/video | Vendor cloud / Windows desktop | Varies     | Varies | GLB/OBJ/USDZ/PLY | Per-scan credits or seat plans. verify: current price per model, upload limits (images, video length, resolution), commercial-use and data-retention terms, whether customer photos may train their models | Good for \"no Mac, no GPU\"; needs account + budget + terms review |","table":"table-1"},"196":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-20","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"| Option                                                                              | Input      | Runs on                   | Thin parts           | Gloss   | Output | Cost                | Verdict                                                                                                                        |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------- | -------------------- | ------- | ------ | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **AI image-to-3D**: TRELLIS (Microsoft, MIT), Hunyuan3D 2.x (Tencent), Tripo, Meshy | 1–4 photos | GPU (open models) or SaaS | **Invents** geometry | Invents | GLB    | Free / SaaS credits | Not for a sales model of *this* bike. OK for placeholders, catalog thumbnails or \"illustrative\" models clearly labeled as such |","table":"table-1"},"197":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-21","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"Notes:"},"198":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-22","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"Object Capture is the only option with **automatic object masking** built in, which matters for\nthe \"background-free\" goal. With COLMAP the bundle needs masking (rembg / U²-Net on the\nphotos before MVS, or cropping the mesh to the dominant cluster after)."},"199":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-23","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"`PhotogrammetrySession` takes a folder URL of images from any camera. EXIF focal length helps.\nDepth and gravity metadata (iPhone LiDAR HEIC) improve scale and orientation. Without them the\nscale is arbitrary and the model may come out tilted, so auto-orient (ROADMAP M2) becomes required."},"200":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-24","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"COLMAP poses are world→camera with OpenCV axes (+X right, +Y down, +Z forward). The viewer\nwants camera→model with camera looking down -Z, +Y up. So:\n`T_c2w = inverse([R|t]) = [Rᵀ | -Rᵀt]`, then flip the camera's Y and Z axes:\n`pose = T_c2w · diag(1, -1, -1, 1)`. COLMAP quaternions are `QW QX QY QZ` (Hamilton,\nworld→camera)."},"201":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-25","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"Splats need a viewer path (Spark / `@sparkjsdev/spark`) and a crop box; pins and areas still work\nbecause they only need a surface to raycast against (a proxy mesh or splat-depth picking)."},"202":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-26","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#recommendation","content":"**Default: Object Capture on a Mac** (`tools/reconstruct/macos/` Swift CLI over an image folder,\nthen package to `bike-capture/1` with `poses.json` from the `.poses` request). It is free, gives the\nbest masked, textured mesh for this object class, and works with photos from any camera and\nwith frames pulled from a video. Detail `.full` for the web (then GLB + decimate), `.raw` only for archiving."},"203":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-27","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#recommendation","content":"**Fallback: COLMAP + OpenMVS in Docker** (Linux / CI / a rented GPU box) for when no Mac is\navailable: same `ingest` → `reconstruct` → `package` flow, plus mesh cropping to the bike.\nExpect worse wheels and paint."},"204":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-28","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#recommendation","content":"**Photoreal later: Gaussian splats** from the same video (COLMAP poses + gsplat/nerfstudio, or\nPolycam/Luma/Scaniverse export) once the viewer loads `.spz`/`.ply` splats."},"205":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-29","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#recommendation","content":"**Cloud API** only after the owner picks a vendor, a budget and accepts its data terms."},"206":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-30","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#recommendation","content":"**AI image-to-3D**: never as \"the bike\". Only for placeholders, clearly labeled."},"207":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-31","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"**Setup**: bike on a stand or a turntable, wheels off the ground or the kickstand hidden; plain\nmatte backdrop that differs from the paint; textured floor or newspaper so the poses solve;\nsoft, even light (two softboxes at 45°, or overcast outdoors), no direct sun, no flash."},"208":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-32","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"**Camera**: any camera ≥ 12 MP; fixed zoom (no zooming between shots); f/8–f/11 for depth of\nfield; ISO as low as possible; shutter ≥ 1/125 s handheld (tripod: anything); lock focus and\nexposure per ring; RAW+JPEG or high-quality JPEG; no portrait mode or beauty filters."},"209":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-33","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"**Shots: 120–200** total, 70–80 % overlap between neighbors:"},"210":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-34","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"Ring 1, hub height (~0.35 m), distance ~1.5–2 m: 36–48 shots (every 7.5–10°)."},"211":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-35","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"Ring 2, saddle height (~0.9 m), looking slightly down: 36–48 shots."},"212":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-36","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"Ring 3, high (~1.6 m), looking down at 45°: 24–36 shots."},"213":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-37","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"Close-ups (0.4–0.6 m), 4–6 shots each, overlapping each other: drivetrain (both sides of the\nrear derailleur, chainring), fork crown and dropouts, cockpit (bar, stem, shifters), saddle and\nseat clamp, each wheel hub and a sector of spokes from both sides."},"214":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-38","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"**Turntable vs walk-around**: turntable with a fixed camera is fastest and steadiest, but the\nbackground must stay out of frame or be masked (static background + rotating bike confuses SfM).\nWalk-around works anywhere and is better for the floor features. Object Capture handles both."},"215":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-39","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"**Reflective paint**: polarizer on the lens (and ideally on the lights), more diffuse light, or a\nremovable dulling spray if the shop agrees. Record which one you used in the manifest notes."},"216":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-40","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-video","content":"**4K (3840×2160) at 30 fps**, or 60 fps if the light allows a fast shutter; HEVC or H.264,\n**not** HDR / Dolby Vision (tone mapping varies between decoders); lock exposure and focus;\nstabilization on; no zooming."},"217":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-41","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-video","content":"**Shutter speed ≥ 1/250 s** (set it in a pro camera app such as Blackmagic Camera; the stock iOS app\npicks it automatically), otherwise motion blur kills features on spokes and cables."},"218":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-42","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-video","content":"**Slow orbit**: about 60–90 s per ring (≈ 4–6°/s), three rings as above, then slow passes over\nthe close-up areas. 3–5 minutes of footage in total."},"219":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-43","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-video","content":"The `ingest` step extracts frames, keeps the sharpest frame per short time window (variance of the\nLaplacian) and only adds a frame when the view has changed enough, aiming for 80–200 frames."},"220":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-44","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#pipeline-planned-shape-toolsreconstruct","content":"Status and the next steps are in ROADMAP.md (Milestone 1.5). For the commands to try\nCOLMAP on Linux today (a CPU-only sparse model, enough to check the poses):"},"221":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-45","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#pipeline-planned-shape-toolsreconstruct","content":"For a dense textured mesh use OpenMVS (`InterfaceCOLMAP` → `DensifyPointCloud` → `ReconstructMesh`\n→ `RefineMesh` → `TextureMesh`) from its Docker image, or COLMAP's dense steps on a CUDA machine."},"222":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-46","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#owner-decisions","content":"See MANUAL-STEPS.md. In short: a Mac (Apple silicon) for the default path;\nwhether to pay for a cloud API (which vendor, monthly budget, OK with its data terms for\ncustomer bikes); a GPU box (rented or owned) for COLMAP dense / splats; whether dulling spray is\nacceptable on customer bikes."},"223":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-47","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#owner-decisions","content":"_Source: `docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md`_"},"224":{"id":"/docs/roadmap","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"page","content":"Roadmap","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Plan"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap"},"225":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-0","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"Milestone 0: Project ops"},"226":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-1","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Milestone 1: Foundation (PR 1)"},"227":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-2","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"Milestone 1.5: Photos & video → 3D"},"228":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-3","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"Milestone 2: Real captures into the viewer"},"229":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-4","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"Milestone 3: Sales experience"},"230":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-5","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"Milestone 4: iOS app depth"},"231":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-6","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"Milestone 5: Backend & multi-bike catalog"},"232":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-7","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"Milestone 6: Quality"},"233":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-8","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"Ideas parking lot"},"234":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-9","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap","content":"The backlog autonomous sessions work through, top to bottom. Each item is sized for one\nsession / one PR. Protocol is in CLAUDE.md."},"235":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-10","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap","content":"Markers: `[ ]` open · `[~]` in progress (draft PR open) · `[x]` done (in an open or merged PR)."},"236":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-11","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[x] **Docs & progress site**: Fumadocs static site (`apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown, with a roadmap progress dashboard and a \"How to test\" guide, published with the viewer to GitHub Pages by `tools/publish-pages.sh` (site at `/bike-3d-brew/`, viewer at `/bike-3d-brew/app/`)."},"237":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-12","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[x] **Auto-publish on develop**: a workflow (`contents: write`) that runs `tools/publish-pages.sh --source develop` on every push to `develop`, so the site stays current even when no agent session runs."},"238":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-13","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[x] **PR previews**: publish each open stack PR under `/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (docs + viewer) and link them from the Progress page, so the owner can test a PR before merging it."},"239":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-14","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[ ] **Prune stale previews**: a scheduled job that removes `/pr/<n>/` for PRs that are no longer open (a missed or failed close run leaves them behind), and squashes gh-pages history once it grows large (each preview adds a full site copy to the branch)."},"240":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-15","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[ ] **Preview link on the PR**: comment (or update one sticky comment) on each PR with its preview URL, so the owner can open it from the GitHub app."},"241":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-16","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Web viewer: three.js, orbit, fly-to areas, background modes (clear / chroma green / studio / dark)"},"242":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-17","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Scene format `bike-scene/1` with validation, local persistence, import/export"},"243":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-18","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Areas (hotspots) and sales comments pinned to the model surface, edit + present modes"},"244":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-19","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Procedural demo bike with seeded areas and comments"},"245":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-20","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"iOS app skeleton: Object Capture (object + area mode), on-device reconstruction, poses, bundle export"},"246":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-21","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"CI: web typecheck/test/build, unsigned iOS build on macOS, Pages deploy workflow"},"247":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-22","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"Top priority: any photo set or video of a bike (any camera) must become a `bike-capture/1` bundle the viewer opens. Research and recommendation: docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md."},"248":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-23","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[x] **Reconstruction research**: options for bikes (Object Capture on macOS, COLMAP + OpenMVS, Meshroom, Gaussian splats, cloud APIs, AI image-to-3D), recommendation, photo and video capture protocols, owner decisions (docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md). Vendor prices/terms still to verify against current pages."},"249":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-24","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **`ingest` CLI** (`tools/reconstruct/`, Node/TS + ffmpeg): photos and videos → sharp, deduplicated, EXIF-upright JPEG frames (variance-of-Laplacian sharpness + novelty selection, 80–200 frames), HEIC → JPEG, coverage report; unit-tested scoring."},"250":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-25","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **COLMAP → `bike-poses/1` conversion**: parse `cameras.txt`/`images.txt`/`points3D.txt`, world→camera OpenCV axes → camera→model −Z/+Y, with tests on synthetic COLMAP output generated from ground truth."},"251":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-26","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **`reconstruct --backend colmap`**: COLMAP + OpenMVS via `tools/reconstruct/docker/` (and native), dense mesh + texture, crop the mesh to the dominant object, optional photo masking (rembg)."},"252":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-27","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **`reconstruct --backend object-capture`**: Swift CLI `tools/reconstruct/macos/` (`PhotogrammetrySession` over an image folder → `model.usdz` + poses), built by a path-filtered macos-latest CI job."},"253":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-28","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **`package`**: result → `bike-capture/1` zip (GLB model, `poses.json`, `images/*.jpg`, manifest with `source: photos|video` and `backend`)."},"254":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-29","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **Synthetic end-to-end eval**: render the fixture bike with texture + textured floor from 60–120 posed cameras and as an orbit video (`tools/fixtures/render-photos.mjs`), run ingest → reconstruct → package, measure pose error after similarity alignment, Chamfer distance / completeness vs ground truth and close-up ranking; report in `docs/RECONSTRUCTION-EVAL.md`."},"255":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-30","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **Web upload flow**: drop a folder of photos or a video on the viewer, send it to a reconstruction backend, open the result."},"256":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-31","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **Cloud backend**: one paid API behind `reconstruct --backend <vendor>` once the owner picks a vendor and budget."},"257":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-32","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **Splats from video**: COLMAP poses + gsplat/nerfstudio → `.spz`, opened through the M6 splat support."},"258":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-33","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Capture bundle import**: drop `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer, unzip in the browser (fflate), load `model.usdz`, read `manifest.json` and `poses.json`, name the scene from the manifest. Unit-test the bundle parser with a synthetic zip."},"259":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-34","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Keep captures across reloads**: cache the unzipped model of the last opened bundles in IndexedDB/OPFS (best effort, quota-aware) so a reload reopens a capture scene without re-dropping the `.bikecapture.zip`."},"260":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-35","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Capture cache on real Safari / iOS**: verify OPFS `createWritable()` vs. the IndexedDB fallback, quota numbers and `persist()` behavior on iPhone Safari and a home-screen web app; tune the 500 MB budget for phones."},"261":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-36","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Cache large models without a main-thread copy**: write models to OPFS from a worker (`createSyncAccessHandle`) or straight from the dropped `File` stream, so a 300 MB capture does not briefly double memory on phones."},"262":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-37","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **USDZ robustness**: three r186 reads binary USDC; `apps/web/src/viewer/usd/` fixes its inline-value decoding, speeds up large meshes ~10×, waits for packed textures and falls back to a `tools/usdz-to-glb.py` hint. Synthetic Object-Capture-like fixtures from `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`."},"263":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-38","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Verify a real Object Capture USDZ**: load a real `model.usdz` (owner's iPhone, see docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md), compare against Quick Look; turn anything off into a fixture-based test (synthetic re-creation, never the capture itself)."},"264":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-39","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Weld USDZ meshes**: three expands face-varying meshes to 3 vertices per triangle (~3M vertices for a 1M-triangle capture); identical corners are merged into an indexed geometry (hash-based, typed arrays, O(n)): 2.9M → 0.49M vertices, 89 → 26 MB of geometry on the 1M-triangle fixture. Decimation stays offline (`tools/optimize-glb.mjs --simplify`). See docs/PERFORMANCE.md."},"265":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-40","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Auto-orient captures**: detect the ground plane / longest horizontal axis so a scanned bike stands upright facing +X; expose rotate/scale/offset controls in Edit mode (writes `model.rotation/scale/offset`)."},"266":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-41","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Auto-orient on real scans**: check the up/front heuristics (`scene/orient.ts`) against real Object Capture bikes (flat bars, kids' bikes, e-bikes with a battery, kickstands); tune the vote weights and add the cases as generated test fixtures."},"267":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-42","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Crop box for area-mode / splat captures**: draggable box in Edit mode that clips everything outside (clipping planes), saved in the scene, so area-mode scans get a clean background."},"268":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-43","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Crop polish**: a rotatable (oriented) crop box for scans whose model-root axes are tilted; a floor-height handle that also re-grounds; show how many comments the crop hides."},"269":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-44","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Photo close-ups per area**: use `poses.json` to find the capture photos that look most directly at each area target (angle + distance score) and show them as a filmstrip under the area; tap to open full screen. HEIC → JPEG conversion at export time on iOS if browsers can't decode HEIC."},"270":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-45","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **iOS JPEG photo export**: write `images/*.jpg` (or a `photos/` folder of 2048 px JPEGs) next to the HEICs in the bundle so Chrome/Firefox skip the 2 MB WASM HEIC decoder and decoding is instant; the web side already prefers whatever decodes natively. Done: `photos/*.jpg` (2048 px, upright) + `manifest.photos`; the web reader uses them when present."},"271":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-46","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Drop the WASM HEIC decoder**: once every exported bundle has `photos/`, remove `libheif-js` (LGPL) or keep it only for old bundles; also check the exported zip size growth (~0.5 MB per photo) on a real capture."},"272":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-47","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Validate close-ups on a real capture**: confirm Object Capture poses share the USDZ frame and the 65° landscape intrinsics assumption (portrait captures, EXIF rotation); read real intrinsics if the iOS app can export them."},"273":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-48","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Occlusion-aware close-ups**: raycast from each candidate camera to the target against the loaded mesh and drop photos where the bike hides it."},"274":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-49","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Pin favourite close-ups**: let staff star photos for an area (the schema already has `Hotspot.photos`) and show starred ones first, also in shared links."},"275":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-50","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[x] **Shareable read-only link**: `?scene=` URL loads a published scene in Present mode with editing hidden; \"Copy share link\" button. Scenes + models served from `apps/web/public/scenes/<id>/`."},"276":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-51","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[x] **Comment polish**: leader lines from pin to card in Present mode, auto-advance/kiosk mode, comment ordering (drag to reorder), markdown-lite (bold, bullet lists) in bodies."},"277":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-52","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Embeddable viewer**: an `embed.html` page + `postMessage` bridge and a `<bike-viewer>` custom element around `mountPresenter` (`present/BikePresenter.ts`), so shops can put a bike on their own site; scope the `styles.css` base rules first so it works inside Shadow DOM."},"278":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-53","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Share docs**: ARCHITECTURE (`bike-share/1`, BikePresenter controller API for the embed), TESTING-GUIDE (try the customer link on a phone), README; mobile E2E run of `share.spec.ts`."},"279":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-54","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Embed packaging**: `embed.html` + postMessage API + `<bike-viewer>` custom element on top of `present/BikePresenter.ts`; scope `styles.css` base rules for Shadow DOM."},"280":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-55","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Hotspot auto-suggest**: for captures, propose default areas (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit, Wheels, Saddle) by letting the user tap each part once; camera view computed from tapped point + local bounds."},"281":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-56","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Spec sheet**: per-bike key specs table (frame material, groupset, weight, sizes) shown in Present mode intro and exported."},"282":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-57","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Branding**: shop logo, accent color and font in scene settings; applied to Present mode."},"283":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-58","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Snapshot / video export**: high-res PNG with transparent or green background; 360° turntable WebM via MediaRecorder for social posts."},"284":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-59","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Undo/redo for the whole scene**: Edit → Model has its own undo stack; extend it to comments and areas (store-level history, Ctrl/Cmd+Z)."},"285":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-60","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Accessibility & i18n pass**: keyboard navigation for pins, focus states, screen-reader labels, number/currency formatting."},"286":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-61","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **In-app viewer**: RealityKit/SceneKit view of `model.usdz` with the same areas and comments (read `bike-scene/1` JSON), so sales staff can present from the phone offline."},"287":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-62","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[x] **Capture guidance for bikes**: checklist overlay (3 orbits: hub height, saddle height, top-down; close-ups of fork crown, dropouts, rear derailleur, cockpit), shot counter per pass, tips for reflective paint (dulling spray / polarizer), turntable support. Done: checklist in the capture screen (orbits ticked by Object Capture's pass detection, close-ups ticked by hand, shots per pass). Turntable: not possible with `ObjectCaptureSession` (ARKit world tracking needs the object still); documented in the app and README."},"288":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-63","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **Turntable capture via the Mac**: a fixed-camera photo mode (plain `AVCapturePhotoOutput` shots while the bike spins on a turntable) reconstructed by `PhotogrammetrySession` on the Mac (see Mac high-detail reconstruction), which accepts turntable sets."},"289":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-64","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **Save the capture checklist**: store ticked close-ups and shots per pass in `record.json` / the manifest so the web side can flag missing close-ups (e.g. \"no derailleur photos\")."},"290":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-65","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **Mac high-detail reconstruction**: `tools/mac-reconstruct` Swift CLI running `PhotogrammetrySession` at `.full` / `.raw` detail from an exported bundle, writing `model.usdz` + `poses.json` back."},"291":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-66","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **On-device GLB export**: convert the USDZ to GLB (ModelIO → glTF writer) so the web viewer never needs conversion."},"292":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-67","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **Upload to viewer**: share sheet target / direct upload of bundles to the web app storage (see Milestone 5)."},"293":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-68","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"[ ] **Catalog page**: list of bikes (cards with turntable thumbnails), search/filter, each opening its scene."},"294":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-69","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"[ ] **Storage**: decide (Cloudflare R2 + Workers, or Supabase) and document; upload bundles, store scenes, auth for editors, public read for shared links."},"295":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-70","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"[ ] **Collaborative comments**: multiple staff editing comments; history."},"296":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-71","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Gaussian splat support**: load `.spz` / splat `.ply` (Scaniverse, Polycam, Luma) via Spark (`@sparkjsdev/spark`) for photoreal paint and chrome; crop box + pins work the same."},"297":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-72","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[x] **Performance**: Draco/Meshopt compression, KTX2 textures, lazy loading, 60 fps on iPhone Safari with 50 pins. Lazily loaded, self-hosted decoders; `tools/optimize-glb.mjs`; BVH picking/occlusion in a worker; budgeted pin updates; device-aware quality (`?quality=low|high`); `tools/bench/` benchmark. See docs/PERFORMANCE.md."},"298":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-73","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Measure on a real iPhone**: first model visible, fps while orbiting with 50 pins and idle CPU in iPhone Safari over 4G (Web Inspector timeline), for a real 20 MB capture and its `optimize-glb` output; record them in docs/PERFORMANCE.md next to the SwiftShader numbers."},"299":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-74","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Runtime decimation for phones**: lazy-load meshoptimizer's simplifier (in a worker) and simplify captures above ~500k triangles on handhelds behind the quality setting, if real-device numbers show the GPU, not fill rate, is the limit."},"300":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-75","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **KTX2/Basis E2E**: an ETC1S/UASTC fixture (needs a Basis encoder in Node, e.g. a WASM build) so the transcoder path is exercised in CI, not only raw KTX2."},"301":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-76","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Progressive capture loading**: show a coarse proxy (or the GLB's first LOD) while a big USDZ parses, and parse/weld it in a worker so the page stays responsive on phones."},"302":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-77","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[x] **E2E tests**: Playwright suite (desktop + iPhone viewport, SwiftShader WebGL) covering view, edit, present, export/import, capture-bundle drop and re-drop, stored captures (reload, Open menu, forget), photo close-ups and lightbox, binary USDC with textures, error toasts, blocked storage, snapshot; synthetic capture-bundle fixtures; unit coverage with ratcheting thresholds; sharded CI job. See docs/TESTING.md."},"303":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-78","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **E2E coverage for app code**: collect V8 coverage from Chromium during the Playwright run (`page.coverage`) and merge it with the unit report, so `ui/app.ts`, `Viewer.ts` and `main.ts` count toward the coverage ratchet."},"304":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-79","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[x] **Render on demand**: only render when the camera, model or pins change (idle stage at 0 fps). Saves phone battery and makes the E2E suite much faster on SwiftShader (today every frame costs ~150–250 ms on CPU)."},"305":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-80","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[x] **WebKit E2E project**: run the suite in Playwright WebKit (closest to iPhone Safari) on a macOS runner or with WebKit's Linux deps; the `mobile` project is Chromium with an iPhone viewport today."},"306":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-81","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **WebKit E2E in CI**: on GitHub's macOS runners (no GPU) every WebKit `page.goto` timed out while the same 45 tests pass locally in 17 s; find a WebGL path that works headless there (or a Linux runner with WebKit deps) and add the job back."},"307":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-82","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Real Safari storage in E2E**: WebKit test contexts have no OPFS, so the WebKit project only exercises the IndexedDB capture cache; cover OPFS in Safari on a real device (see the \"Capture cache on real Safari / iOS\" item)."},"308":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-83","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **One fixture generator**: fold `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` (GLB bundle for the Pages sample) and `tools/fixtures/make-capture.mjs` (USDZ bundle with photo poses) into `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs` as variants, so there is one bike geometry and one pose layout to maintain."},"309":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-84","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **HEIC in E2E**: a small synthetic HEIC photo fixture (needs an encoder at generation time) so the libheif worker path is exercised in Chromium."},"310":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-85","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Docs**: end-to-end guide with screenshots: capture → build → export → annotate → share."},"311":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-86","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"AR \"place the bike in your room\" via Quick Look (`model.usdz` + `<a rel=\"ar\">`)."},"312":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-87","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"Compare two bikes side by side."},"313":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-88","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"Size guide overlay (rider silhouette to scale)."},"314":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-89","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"Measure tool (tap two points → distance in mm)."},"315":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-90","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"_Source: `ROADMAP.md`_"},"316":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"page","content":"How to test","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide"},"317":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-0","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"On your phone (no setup)"},"318":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-1","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-a-laptop","content":"On a laptop"},"319":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-2","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide#make-a-synthetic-capture-bundle","content":"Make a synthetic capture bundle"},"320":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-3","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"What each PR adds"},"321":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-4","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide","content":"A short guide for the owner: how to try what the agents built, on a phone or a laptop. Every\nPR that adds something testable extends the \"What each PR adds\" table at the bottom."},"322":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-5","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"Open the live demo: **https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/**\n(this site lives one level up: https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/)."},"323":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-6","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"The procedural demo bike loads with sample areas and comments."},"324":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-7","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"**View**: drag to orbit, pinch to zoom, tap an area chip (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit…) to fly there."},"325":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-8","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"**Edit**: tap the bike to drop a comment pin; save the current camera as a new area."},"326":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-9","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"**Present**: steps through the areas one by one, as you would with a customer."},"327":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-10","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"The background buttons switch between clear, chroma green, studio and dark."},"328":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-11","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"To try a capture bundle without the iPhone app, download the synthetic one:\n**https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/samples/synthetic-bike.bikecapture.zip**,\nthen in the viewer tap **Open…** and pick it from Files. A red low-poly bike replaces the demo\nand the scene is named \"Synthetic test bike\"."},"329":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-12","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"The site is republished automatically on every push to the stack tip (the newest open PR nothing else is stacked on, or `develop` when none is open). Each open PR also gets its\nown copy at `https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (viewer at `/pr/<n>/app/`),\nlisted under **PR previews** on the home and Progress pages, so you can try a PR before\nmerging it. The home page says which commit and branch it was built from."},"330":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-13","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-a-laptop","content":"Checks the agents run on every PR (CI runs them too):"},"331":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-14","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-a-laptop","content":"How the automated tests work and how to add them: Testing."},"332":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-15","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#make-a-synthetic-capture-bundle","content":"The iPhone app exports `*.bikecapture.zip` (format `bike-capture/1`, see\nArchitecture). To test the import path without a phone:"},"333":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-16","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#make-a-synthetic-capture-bundle","content":"It writes a low-poly bike as `model.glb`, a `manifest.json`, an orbit of camera poses in\n`poses.json` and no photos, all nested in one folder like the real export. Drag the file onto\nthe viewer (or use **Open…**). Dropping the same file again later restores the comments you\nadded to it."},"334":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-17","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#make-a-synthetic-capture-bundle","content":"With a real capture: AirDrop the `.bikecapture.zip` from the iPhone to the laptop and drop it on\nthe viewer. If the model does not show, note what the viewer says and add it to\nManual steps."},"335":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-18","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR            | What to try                                                                           |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #1 Foundation | Demo bike, areas, comments, Edit and Present modes, background switcher, Export JSON. |","table":"table-0"},"336":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-19","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                       | What to try                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #2 Capture bundle import | **Open…** the synthetic bundle above (or drop it on desktop): it loads and is named from the manifest. Add a comment, reload, open the same file again: the comment is back. |","table":"table-0"},"337":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-20","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR        | What to try                                                                     |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docs site | This site: the home page shows roadmap progress; **Progress** lists every item. |","table":"table-0"},"338":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-21","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #7 Test system | Nothing new to click: `npm run e2e` drives the real viewer through every flow above (demo, edit, present, export/import, capture bundles, stored captures, photo close-ups, error toasts) at desktop and iPhone sizes; `npm run test:coverage` shows unit coverage. The suite found and fixed a bug where a tap right after jumping to an area (with reduced motion on) missed the bike. |","table":"table-0"},"339":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-22","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #9 Auto-orient | Make a tilted bundle (`node tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs --out tilted.bikecapture.zip`) and **Open…** it: the bike stands up facing right and the toast says \"Auto-oriented\". In **Edit → Model** try Undo (back to lying on its side), Auto-orient, the rotate ±90° buttons, Turn 180°, and type a real length in cm. Pin a comment first: it stays on the same spot through every rotation. |","table":"table-0"},"340":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-23","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR           | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #10 Crop box | Make an area-mode bundle with a floor and clutter (`node tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs --out area.bikecapture.zip --rotate 0,0,0 --offset 0,0,0 --ground --mode area`) and **Open…** it: the toast suggests cropping. In **Edit → Model → Crop** turn the crop on, press **Fit to bike** (floor and crate disappear), then drag a face handle with the mouse or a finger: the camera must not orbit while dragging. Comments can't be pinned on cropped-away parts, and pins outside the box hide. |","table":"table-0"},"341":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-24","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                      | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #8 Share with customers | Open the published demo as a customer: `/bike-3d-brew/app/?scene=scenes/demo/scene.bike.json&view=present` (on your phone too). Swipe between areas, tap a pin (leader line to its card), add `&kiosk=1&interval=4` for auto-play that pauses when you touch it. In the editor, **Share** on a published scene copies the link; on a local capture it exports a `.bikeshare.zip` that `node tools/publish-scene.mjs <zip>` installs. In Edit mode, drag comments to reorder them and use **bold**, *italic* and `- ` lists in bodies. |","table":"table-0"},"342":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-25","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR              | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #12 Performance | Orbit the demo, then let go: the camera glides to a stop and the page goes quiet (DevTools → Performance shows no frames while idle). Pins slide with the bike and dim when the bike is in front of them. On a phone, open a large capture: it appears, then picking a comment point is instant. Add `?quality=low` to the URL for the cheapest rendering. A GLB made with `node tools/optimize-glb.mjs in.glb out.glb` opens like any other. |","table":"table-0"},"343":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-26","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                                     | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #14 iOS capture guidance + JPEG photos | On the iPhone: during a capture tap **Checklist**: orbits tick themselves after each completed pass, close-ups tick on tap, the top bar shows shots for the current pass. Export a bundle: the zip has `photos/*.jpg` next to `images/*.HEIC` and `manifest.json` has `\"photos\": \"photos/\"`. Open it in desktop Chrome: close-up photos appear without the HEIC decoder (no `heic` worker request in DevTools → Network). Web side alone: `npm test` (capture.test.ts covers the `photos/` preference). |","table":"table-0"},"344":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-27","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #16 WebKit E2E | Nothing new to click. On a Mac: `npx playwright install webkit && npm run e2e:webkit` runs the iPhone flows in Safari's engine (45 tests). Open the customer link in Safari on your phone: no console error when the Present card changes height. |","table":"table-0"},"345":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-28","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #15 Auto-publish + PR previews | Open the home page: **PR previews** lists open PRs with Viewer and Docs links; open `/bike-3d-brew/pr/15/app/` and the demo bike loads. Push to a PR and its preview updates a few minutes later (Actions → \"PR preview\"); close it and it disappears from the list. Merging into `develop` updates the main site (Actions → \"Publish site\"). |","table":"table-0"},"346":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-29","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #17 Site follows the stack tip | The home page has no credits box any more. Push to the top PR of the stack (or press *Run workflow* on Actions → \"Publish site\" from it): the main site shows that branch a few minutes later (the footer names it). Pushes to other branches skip publishing. |","table":"table-0"},"347":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-30","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"_Source: `docs/TESTING-GUIDE.md`_"},"348":{"id":"/docs/testing","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"page","content":"Testing","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing"},"349":{"id":"/docs/testing-0","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"Unit tests"},"350":{"id":"/docs/testing-1","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"What is not unit-tested, and why"},"351":{"id":"/docs/testing-2","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#coverage","content":"Coverage"},"352":{"id":"/docs/testing-3","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"Fixtures"},"353":{"id":"/docs/testing-4","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"`make-capture-bundle.mjs`"},"354":{"id":"/docs/testing-5","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#rendered-photo-bundle","content":"Rendered-photo bundle"},"355":{"id":"/docs/testing-6","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#end-to-end-tests","content":"End-to-end tests"},"356":{"id":"/docs/testing-7","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"The `window.__bike` test hook"},"357":{"id":"/docs/testing-8","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Writing reliable E2E tests"},"358":{"id":"/docs/testing-9","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"What the suite covers"},"359":{"id":"/docs/testing-10","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"Three layers, cheapest first. CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs all of them on every PR."},"360":{"id":"/docs/testing-11","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"| Layer | Where                     | Runs in                                        | Command    |\n| ----- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| Unit  | `apps/web/test/*.test.ts` | Vitest, Node (happy-dom per file where needed) | `npm test` |","table":"table-0"},"361":{"id":"/docs/testing-12","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"| Layer    | Where                   | Runs in | Command                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----------------------- |\n| Coverage | same tests, V8 coverage | Vitest  | `npm run test:coverage` |","table":"table-0"},"362":{"id":"/docs/testing-13","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"| Layer      | Where                    | Runs in                                  | Command       |\n| ---------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| End-to-end | `apps/web/e2e/*.spec.ts` | Playwright, Chromium + SwiftShader WebGL | `npm run e2e` |","table":"table-0"},"363":{"id":"/docs/testing-14","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"Fixtures for both come from one generator: `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`."},"364":{"id":"/docs/testing-15","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"Pure logic lives in `apps/web/src/scene/` (scene format, store, camera math, capture bundles,\nUI helpers in `helpers.ts`) and is tested in plain Node. When UI code grows a decision (a\ndefault, a message, a URL rule), move it into `src/scene/helpers.ts` and test it there."},"365":{"id":"/docs/testing-16","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"three.js code that needs no WebGL (loaders, `centerOnGround`, the demo bike's geometry) is\ntested in Node too (`viewer-node.test.ts`). three's `FileLoader` needs a `ProgressEvent`\nstub in Node; the test file installs one. Models are passed as `data:` URLs."},"366":{"id":"/docs/testing-17","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"DOM code (`ui/dom.ts`, `viewer/pins.ts`, `ui/photoViewer.ts`, `ui/photoLibrary.ts`,\n`ui/photoDecode.ts`) opts into happy-dom with a first-line comment\n`// @vitest-environment happy-dom`. Browser APIs happy-dom lacks are stubbed per test:\n`createImageBitmap`, `<img>.decode`, `OffscreenCanvas`, `Worker` (photoDecode), pointer capture\n(lightbox gestures), a fake `Viewer` (pins). Decoding itself is mocked in `photoLibrary.test.ts`."},"367":{"id":"/docs/testing-18","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"Storage: `storage/backends.ts` runs against `fake-indexeddb` and a small in-memory OPFS\n(`FakeDir` in `backends.test.ts`); `navigator` is replaced with `vi.stubGlobal`."},"368":{"id":"/docs/testing-19","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"Zip parsing: `zipIndex.test.ts` hand-builds zips byte by byte (zip64 records and extra fields,\nforeign extras, odd methods, lying sizes), branches fflate never writes."},"369":{"id":"/docs/testing-20","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"USD: `usdz.test.ts` loads the committed binary USDC fixtures (`apps/web/test/fixtures/`, made\nby `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py` with Pixar USD); `usd-units.test.ts` drives the crate\ndecoders and composer fast paths directly for encodings the fixtures do not contain."},"370":{"id":"/docs/testing-21","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"Excluded from coverage in `apps/web/vite.config.ts`, each covered by the E2E suite instead:"},"371":{"id":"/docs/testing-22","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File          | Why it cannot run in Node                |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `src/main.ts` | page bootstrap: the whole DOM plus WebGL |","table":"table-1"},"372":{"id":"/docs/testing-23","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File            | Why it cannot run in Node                |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `src/ui/app.ts` | UI controller driving the WebGL `Viewer` |","table":"table-1"},"373":{"id":"/docs/testing-24","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File                   | Why it cannot run in Node                          |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/viewer/Viewer.ts` | `WebGLRenderer`, `OrbitControls`, `ResizeObserver` |","table":"table-1"},"374":{"id":"/docs/testing-25","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File                    | Why it cannot run in Node         |\n| ----------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `src/ui/heic.worker.ts` | a Web Worker running libheif WASM |","table":"table-1"},"375":{"id":"/docs/testing-26","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File            | Why it cannot run in Node |\n| --------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `src/**/*.d.ts` | type declarations only    |","table":"table-1"},"376":{"id":"/docs/testing-27","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#coverage","content":"`npm run test:coverage` writes `coverage/` (text summary, HTML report, `coverage-summary.json`).\nThresholds in `apps/web/vite.config.ts` are a ratchet set just under the current numbers,\nglobally and for `src/scene/**`; CI fails when coverage drops below them (and the web job\nprints the totals in its step summary). At the time of writing: lines 99.8%, statements 98.9%,\nfunctions 98%, branches 92.8%. When you raise\ncoverage, raise the thresholds in the same PR. Never lower them to make a PR pass."},"377":{"id":"/docs/testing-28","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"Four generators, each with a job. All output is synthetic; no real capture is ever committed."},"378":{"id":"/docs/testing-29","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"| Generator                                | Output                                                              | Used by                                                                           |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs` | the bundle variants below (USDZ, GLB, flat, broken…), deterministic | E2E (global setup), `fixtures.test.ts`, `viewer-node.test.ts`, `npm run fixtures` |","table":"table-2"},"379":{"id":"/docs/testing-30","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"| Generator                                                 | Output                                                                                                          | Used by                                                                                                            |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-capture.mjs` (+ `render-photos.mjs`) | a USDZ bundle off-origin like a real reconstruction, orbit + close-up poses, placeholder or **rendered** photos | `photos.test.ts`, `capture.test.ts`, E2E photo close-ups (`bike-photos.bikecapture.zip`), `npm run fixture:photos` |","table":"table-2"},"380":{"id":"/docs/testing-31","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"| Generator                     | Output                                                                       | Used by                                                                         |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py` | binary USDC (crate) packages in `apps/web/test/fixtures/` (committed, small) | `usdz.test.ts`, E2E \"binary USDC loads textured\"; needs Pixar USD to regenerate |","table":"table-2"},"381":{"id":"/docs/testing-32","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"| Generator                    | Output                           | Used by                                                                 |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` | GLB bundle \"Synthetic test bike\" | the sample on the Pages site (`tools/publish-pages.sh`), manual testing |","table":"table-2"},"382":{"id":"/docs/testing-33","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"Folding the three JS generators into one is a ROADMAP follow-up."},"383":{"id":"/docs/testing-34","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"`buildFixtures()` returns every fixture as bytes and is also imported by unit tests. Output is\nbyte-for-byte deterministic (fixed zip timestamps, rounded floats), so nothing binary is\ncommitted. What it makes:"},"384":{"id":"/docs/testing-35","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                   | What it exercises                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike.bikecapture.zip` | iOS layout (everything under one folder): manifest, ASCII-USD `model.usdz` of a low-poly vertex-colored bike (wheels, frame tubes, fork, cockpit, saddle, drivetrain as named meshes), `poses.json` with 32 cameras on three rings looking at the bike, 32 tiny placeholder PNG photos, `record.json` |","table":"table-3"},"385":{"id":"/docs/testing-36","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                       | What it exercises                                                |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike-glb.bikecapture.zip` | same bike as GLB (three's `GLTFExporter` in Node, vertex colors) |","table":"table-3"},"386":{"id":"/docs/testing-37","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                        | What it exercises                    |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `bike-flat.bikecapture.zip` | flat zip with Finder `__MACOSX` junk |","table":"table-3"},"387":{"id":"/docs/testing-38","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                                | What it exercises                          |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `bike-broken-poses.bikecapture.zip` | invalid `poses.json`: opens with a warning |","table":"table-3"},"388":{"id":"/docs/testing-39","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                            | What it exercises                  |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `bike-no-model.bikecapture.zip` | capture never reconstructed: error |","table":"table-3"},"389":{"id":"/docs/testing-40","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                        | What it exercises              |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `not-a-zip.bikecapture.zip` | text with a `.zip` name: error |","table":"table-3"},"390":{"id":"/docs/testing-41","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                    | What it exercises |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `bike.usdz`, `bike.glb` | bare model files  |","table":"table-3"},"391":{"id":"/docs/testing-42","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"The photos are PNG stand-ins: real captures have HEIC, which Node cannot encode."},"392":{"id":"/docs/testing-43","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#rendered-photo-bundle","content":"The E2E global setup (`apps/web/e2e/global-setup.ts`) also renders the `make-capture.mjs` bike\nfrom each of its poses with `render-photos.mjs` (headless Chromium, three.js, the iPhone wide\ncamera's field of view) and writes `bike-photos.bikecapture.zip`, so photo close-ups are ranked\nand shown from real images of the fixture."},"393":{"id":"/docs/testing-44","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#end-to-end-tests","content":"Playwright drives the **production build** (`vite build` + `vite preview` on port 4190, started\nby the config's `webServer`) in two projects: `desktop` (1280×800, every spec) and `mobile`\n(iPhone 14 viewport with touch, DPR 1 to keep CPU rendering fast; only the specs where layout and\ntouch matter: view, edit, present, photos). WebGL runs on SwiftShader\n(`--use-angle=swiftshader --enable-unsafe-swiftshader`), so no GPU is needed. CI splits the\nsuite into two parallel shards (`--shard=1/2`, `2/2`)."},"394":{"id":"/docs/testing-45","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#end-to-end-tests","content":"A third project, `webkit`, runs the iPhone 14 profile in Playwright's WebKit (the engine of iPhone\nSafari) over the view, edit, present, photos, share and files specs. It is opt-in\n(`npm run e2e:webkit`, after `npx playwright install webkit`; the global setup also needs Chromium, which renders the photo fixtures) and local-only for now: on GitHub's\nGPU-less macOS runners every WebKit page load timed out (WebGL), see ROADMAP. It found two\nSafari-only issues: a \"ResizeObserver loop\" page error from the Present card's height update\n(now applied on the next frame), and test contexts without OPFS, where captures use the\nIndexedDB fallback."},"395":{"id":"/docs/testing-46","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#end-to-end-tests","content":"Browser: CI runs `npx playwright install --with-deps --only-shell chromium`. On a machine with a\npreinstalled Chromium (e.g. the agent containers: `/opt/pw-browsers/chromium`), do not run\n`playwright install`; set `PW_CHROMIUM_PATH=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium` and the config uses it as\n`launchOptions.executablePath`. `@playwright/test` is pinned to the version whose browsers are\npreinstalled there."},"396":{"id":"/docs/testing-47","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"`main.ts` exposes `window.__bike = { app, store, viewer, ready }` only in the dev server or when\nthe URL has `?e2e` (the suite always adds it). Tests use it to:"},"397":{"id":"/docs/testing-48","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"wait for state instead of sleeping: `ready` (boot finished), a model in `viewer.modelRoot`,\n`viewer.flying` (camera animation running);"},"398":{"id":"/docs/testing-49","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"find a point on the model to tap: `modelPoint()` in `e2e/helpers.ts` asks the app's own\n`viewer.pick()` and checks `document.elementFromPoint` so the tap lands on the canvas, not a pin;"},"399":{"id":"/docs/testing-50","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"read the scene for assertions (`store.scene`)."},"400":{"id":"/docs/testing-51","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"Everything else goes through the real UI: clicks, taps, keys, the file picker\n(`setInputFiles`), real `DragEvent` drops with a `DataTransfer`, dialogs and downloads. Keep the\nhook read-mostly; if a test needs to mutate app state through it, that is a sign a UI path is\nmissing."},"401":{"id":"/docs/testing-52","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Never `waitForTimeout`. Wait on app state (`waitForFunction`, `expect.poll`) or on web-first\nassertions (`toHaveText`, `toHaveCount`, `toHaveAttribute`)."},"402":{"id":"/docs/testing-53","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Camera flights are instant because the suite emulates `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, which\nthe viewer honors; a test that wants the animation calls\n`page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion: 'no-preference' })` and waits for `viewer.flying === false`."},"403":{"id":"/docs/testing-54","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Use `collectErrors(page)` and assert it is empty where a flow should be clean."},"404":{"id":"/docs/testing-55","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Screenshots are for humans: `snap(page, testInfo, name)` saves to `test-results/` and attaches\nto the HTML report. Do not add pixel-diff assertions; SwiftShader output differs across\nmachines."},"405":{"id":"/docs/testing-56","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Tests run in parallel across fresh browser contexts, so each test starts from an empty\n`localStorage` and the seeded demo."},"406":{"id":"/docs/testing-57","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"On CI a failing run uploads `playwright-report/` and `test-results/` (traces, screenshots) as\nthe `playwright-report` artifact. CI retries once; a test that only passes on retry is reported\nas flaky and should be fixed, not ignored."},"407":{"id":"/docs/testing-58","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`view.spec.ts`: demo loads with seeded areas/comments/pins and no console errors; fly to an\narea and back; comment focus; background modes (and the chroma-green opaque clear); Snapshot\ndownloads a real PNG; Reset view."},"408":{"id":"/docs/testing-59","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`edit.spec.ts`: add/edit/delete a comment picked on the canvas; persistence across reload;\nCancel/Escape; default area; save/rename/set view/delete areas; bike details."},"409":{"id":"/docs/testing-60","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`present.spec.ts`: keys (←, →, space, Esc) and ‹ › buttons with wrap-around; `?mode=present`."},"410":{"id":"/docs/testing-61","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`files.spec.ts`: export JSON → re-import; `?scene=` published scene (routed); capture bundles\nvia picker and drag-and-drop (USDZ, GLB, flat); re-drop after reload restores comments;\nbroken poses warning; bare model drop; error toasts for seven kinds of bad files."},"411":{"id":"/docs/testing-62","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`storage.spec.ts`: everything still works with `localStorage` throwing."},"412":{"id":"/docs/testing-63","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`capture-cache.spec.ts`: a reload reopens the last capture from OPFS with its comments; the\nOpen menu lists stored captures (most recent first, size, current one marked), switches between\nthem, closes on Esc / outside click, \"Choose a file…\", forgets them; forgotten means a reload\nasks for the zip again. `files.spec.ts` keeps the re-drop flow with capture storage blocked\n(`blockCaptureStorage()`)."},"413":{"id":"/docs/testing-64","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`photos.spec.ts`: a saved area shows its best photos (all thumbnails decode), the lightbox\nsteps with ←/→ and ‹ › with wrap-around, Esc closes only the lightbox; Present mode shows the\nstrip; after a reload the thumbnails come from browser storage."},"414":{"id":"/docs/testing-65","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`files.spec.ts` also drops the committed binary USDC fixture and checks it renders with its\ndiffuse and normal textures decoded."},"415":{"id":"/docs/testing-66","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`perf.spec.ts`: an idle stage renders 0 frames, orbiting renders and stops again with pins moved, canvas snapshots work without a preserved drawing buffer, and Meshopt / Draco / KTX2 GLBs (from `tools/fixtures/make-compressed-glb.mjs`) open with self-hosted decoders and no foreign requests."},"416":{"id":"/docs/testing-67","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"The viewer renders on demand: to wait for a picture to settle use `viewer.rendering === false`; `viewer.renderCount` counts drawn frames."},"417":{"id":"/docs/testing-68","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/t