":382,"393":337,"394":235,"395":243,"396":147,"397":404,"398":273,"399":345,"400":270,"401":309,"402":244,"403":403,"404":358,"405":375,"406":318,"407":160,"408":144,"409":154,"410":146,"411":156,"412":141,"413":153,"414":145,"415":151,"416":389,"417":7},"orderedDocs":[[89,"_Source: `CHANGELOG.md`_"],[65,"_Source: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`_"],[107,"_Source: `docs/GOALS.md`_"],[134,"_Source: `docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md`_"],[172,"_Source: `docs/PERFORMANCE.md`_"],[223,"_Source: `docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md`_"],[347,"_Source: `docs/TESTING-GUIDE.md`_"],[417,"_Source: `docs/TESTING.md`_"],[114,"_Source: `README.md`_"],[315,"_Source: `ROADMAP.md`_"],[249,"[ ] **`ingest` CLI** (`tools/reconstruct/`, Node/TS + ffmpeg): photos and videos → sharp, deduplicated, EXIF-upright JPEG frames (variance-of-Laplacian sharpness + novelty selection, 80–200 frames), HEIC → JPEG, coverage report; unit-tested scoring."],[253,"[ ] **`package`**: result → `bike-capture/1` zip (GLB model, `poses.json`, `images/*.jpg`, manifest with `source: photos|video` and `backend`)."],[251,"[ ] **`reconstruct --backend colmap`**: COLMAP + OpenMVS via `tools/reconstruct/docker/` (and native), dense mesh + texture, crop the mesh to the dominant object, optional photo masking (rembg)."],[252,"[ ] **`reconstruct --backend object-capture`**: Swift CLI `tools/reconstruct/macos/` (`PhotogrammetrySession` over an image folder → `model.usdz` + poses), built by a path-filtered macos-latest CI job."],[285,"[ ] **Accessibility & i18n pass**: keyboard navigation for pins, focus states, screen-reader labels, number/currency formatting."],[266,"[ ] **Auto-orient on real scans**: check the up/front heuristics (`scene/orient.ts`) against real Object Capture bikes (flat bars, kids' bikes, e-bikes with a battery, kickstands); tune the vote weights and add the cases as generated test fixtures."],[282,"[ ] **Branding**: shop logo, accent color and font in scene settings; applied to Present mode."],[261,"[ ] **Cache large models without a main-thread copy**: write models to OPFS from a worker (`createSyncAccessHandle`) or straight from the dropped `File` stream, so a 300 MB capture does not briefly double memory on phones."],[260,"[ ] **Capture cache on real Safari / iOS**: verify OPFS `createWritable()` vs. the IndexedDB fallback, quota numbers and `persist()` behavior on iPhone Safari and a home-screen web app; tune the 500 MB budget for phones."],[293,"[ ] **Catalog page**: list of bikes (cards with turntable thumbnails), search/filter, each opening its scene."],[256,"[ ] **Cloud backend**: one paid API behind `reconstruct --backend <vendor>` once the owner picks a vendor and budget."],[295,"[ ] **Collaborative comments**: multiple staff editing comments; history."],[250,"[ ] **COLMAP → `bike-poses/1` conversion**: parse `cameras.txt`/`images.txt`/`points3D.txt`, world→camera OpenCV axes → camera→model −Z/+Y, with tests on synthetic COLMAP output generated from ground truth."],[268,"[ ] **Crop polish**: a rotatable (oriented) crop box for scans whose model-root axes are tilted; a floor-height handle that also re-grounds; show how many comments the crop hides."],[310,"[ ] **Docs**: end-to-end guide with screenshots: capture → build → export → annotate → share."],[271,"[ ] **Drop the WASM HEIC decoder**: once every exported bundle has `photos/`, remove `libheif-js` (LGPL) or keep it only for old bundles; also check the exported zip size growth (~0.5 MB per photo) on a real capture."],[303,"[ ] **E2E coverage for app code**: collect V8 coverage from Chromium during the Playwright run (`page.coverage`) and merge it with the unit report, so `ui/app.ts`, `Viewer.ts` and `main.ts` count toward the coverage ratchet."],[279,"[ ] **Embed packaging**: `embed.html` + postMessage API + `<bike-viewer>` custom element on top of `present/BikePresenter.ts`; scope `styles.css` base rules for Shadow DOM."],[277,"[ ] **Embeddable viewer**: an `embed.html` page + `postMessage` bridge and a `<bike-viewer>` custom element around `mountPresenter` (`present/BikePresenter.ts`), so shops can put a bike on their own site; scope the `styles.css` base rules first so it works inside Shadow DOM."],[296,"[ ] **Gaussian splat support**: load `.spz` / splat `.ply` (Scaniverse, Polycam, Luma) via Spark (`@sparkjsdev/spark`) for photoreal paint and chrome; crop box + pins work the same."],[309,"[ ] **HEIC in E2E**: a small synthetic HEIC photo fixture (needs an encoder at generation time) so the libheif worker path is exercised in Chromium."],[280,"[ ] **Hotspot auto-suggest**: for captures, propose default areas (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit, Wheels, Saddle) by letting the user tap each part once; camera view computed from tapped point + local bounds."],[286,"[ ] **In-app viewer**: RealityKit/SceneKit view of `model.usdz` with the same areas and comments (read `bike-scene/1` JSON), so sales staff can present from the phone offline."],[300,"[ ] **KTX2/Basis E2E**: an ETC1S/UASTC fixture (needs a Basis encoder in Node, e.g. a WASM build) so the transcoder path is exercised in CI, not only raw KTX2."],[290,"[ ] **Mac high-detail reconstruction**: `tools/mac-reconstruct` Swift CLI running `PhotogrammetrySession` at `.full` / `.raw` detail from an exported bundle, writing `model.usdz` + `poses.json` back."],[298,"[ ] **Measure on a real iPhone**: first model visible, fps while orbiting with 50 pins and idle CPU in iPhone Safari over 4G (Web Inspector timeline), for a real 20 MB capture and its `optimize-glb` output; record them in docs/PERFORMANCE.md next to the SwiftShader numbers."],[273,"[ ] **Occlusion-aware close-ups**: raycast from each candidate camera to the target against the loaded mesh and drop photos where the bike hides it."],[291,"[ ] **On-device GLB export**: convert the USDZ to GLB (ModelIO → glTF writer) so the web viewer never needs conversion."],[308,"[ ] **One fixture generator**: fold `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` (GLB bundle for the Pages sample) and `tools/fixtures/make-capture.mjs` (USDZ bundle with photo poses) into `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs` as variants, so there is one bike geometry and one pose layout to maintain."],[274,"[ ] **Pin favourite close-ups**: let staff star photos for an area (the schema already has `Hotspot.photos`) and show starred ones first, also in shared links."],[240,"[ ] **Preview link on the PR**: comment (or update one sticky comment) on each PR with its preview URL, so the owner can open it from the GitHub app."],[301,"[ ] **Progressive capture loading**: show a coarse proxy (or the GLB's first LOD) while a big USDZ parses, and parse/weld it in a worker so the page stays responsive on phones."],[239,"[ ] **Prune stale previews**: a scheduled job that removes `/pr/<n>/` for PRs that are no longer open (a missed or failed close run leaves them behind), and squashes gh-pages history once it grows large (each preview adds a full site copy to the branch)."],[307,"[ ] **Real Safari storage in E2E**: WebKit test contexts have no OPFS, so the WebKit project only exercises the IndexedDB capture cache; cover OPFS in Safari on a real device (see the \"Capture cache on real Safari / iOS\" item)."],[299,"[ ] **Runtime decimation for phones**: lazy-load meshoptimizer's simplifier (in a worker) and simplify captures above ~500k triangles on handhelds behind the quality setting, if real-device numbers show the GPU, not fill rate, is the limit."],[289,"[ ] **Save the capture checklist**: store ticked close-ups and shots per pass in `record.json` / the manifest so the web side can flag missing close-ups (e.g. \"no derailleur photos\")."],[278,"[ ] **Share docs**: ARCHITECTURE (`bike-share/1`, BikePresenter controller API for the embed), TESTING-GUIDE (try the customer link on a phone), README; mobile E2E run of `share.spec.ts`."],[283,"[ ] **Snapshot / video export**: high-res PNG with transparent or green background; 360° turntable WebM via MediaRecorder for social posts."],[281,"[ ] **Spec sheet**: per-bike key specs table (frame material, groupset, weight, sizes) shown in Present mode intro and exported."],[257,"[ ] **Splats from video**: COLMAP poses + gsplat/nerfstudio → `.spz`, opened through the M6 splat support."],[294,"[ ] **Storage**: decide (Cloudflare R2 + Workers, or Supabase) and document; upload bundles, store scenes, auth for editors, public read for shared links."],[254,"[ ] **Synthetic end-to-end eval**: render the fixture bike with texture + textured floor from 60–120 posed cameras and as an orbit video (`tools/fixtures/render-photos.mjs`), run ingest → reconstruct → package, measure pose error after similarity alignment, Chamfer distance / completeness vs ground truth and close-up ranking; report in `docs/RECONSTRUCTION-EVAL.md`."],[288,"[ ] **Turntable capture via the Mac**: a fixed-camera photo mode (plain `AVCapturePhotoOutput` shots while the bike spins on a turntable) reconstructed by `PhotogrammetrySession` on the Mac (see Mac high-detail reconstruction), which accepts turntable sets."],[284,"[ ] **Undo/redo for the whole scene**: Edit → Model has its own undo stack; extend it to comments and areas (store-level history, Ctrl/Cmd+Z)."],[292,"[ ] **Upload to viewer**: share sheet target / direct upload of bundles to the web app storage (see Milestone 5)."],[272,"[ ] **Validate close-ups on a real capture**: confirm Object Capture poses share the USDZ frame and the 65° landscape intrinsics assumption (portrait captures, EXIF rotation); read real intrinsics if the iOS app can export them."],[263,"[ ] **Verify a real Object Capture USDZ**: load a real `model.usdz` (owner's iPhone, see docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md), compare against Quick Look; turn anything off into a fixture-based test (synthetic re-creation, never the capture itself)."],[255,"[ ] **Web upload flow**: drop a folder of photos or a video on the viewer, send it to a reconstruction backend, open the result."],[306,"[ ] **WebKit E2E in CI**: on GitHub's macOS runners (no GPU) every WebKit `page.goto` timed out while the same 45 tests pass locally in 17 s; find a WebGL path that works headless there (or a Linux runner with WebKit deps) and add the job back."],[265,"[x] **Auto-orient captures**: detect the ground plane / longest horizontal axis so a scanned bike stands upright facing +X; expose rotate/scale/offset controls in Edit mode (writes `model.rotation/scale/offset`)."],[237,"[x] **Auto-publish on develop**: a workflow (`contents: write`) that runs `tools/publish-pages.sh --source develop` on every push to `develop`, so the site stays current even when no agent session runs."],[258,"[x] **Capture bundle import**: drop `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer, unzip in the browser (fflate), load `model.usdz`, read `manifest.json` and `poses.json`, name the scene from the manifest. Unit-test the bundle parser with a synthetic zip."],[287,"[x] **Capture guidance for bikes**: checklist overlay (3 orbits: hub height, saddle height, top-down; close-ups of fork crown, dropouts, rear derailleur, cockpit), shot counter per pass, tips for reflective paint (dulling spray / polarizer), turntable support. Done: checklist in the capture screen (orbits ticked by Object Capture's pass detection, close-ups ticked by hand, shots per pass). Turntable: not possible with `ObjectCaptureSession` (ARKit world tracking needs the object still); documented in the app and README."],[276,"[x] **Comment polish**: leader lines from pin to card in Present mode, auto-advance/kiosk mode, comment ordering (drag to reorder), markdown-lite (bold, bullet lists) in bodies."],[267,"[x] **Crop box for area-mode / splat captures**: draggable box in Edit mode that clips everything outside (clipping planes), saved in the scene, so area-mode scans get a clean background."],[236,"[x] **Docs & progress site**: Fumadocs static site (`apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown, with a roadmap progress dashboard and a \"How to test\" guide, published with the viewer to GitHub Pages by `tools/publish-pages.sh` (site at `/bike-3d-brew/`, viewer at `/bike-3d-brew/app/`)."],[302,"[x] **E2E tests**: Playwright suite (desktop + iPhone viewport, SwiftShader WebGL) covering view, edit, present, export/import, capture-bundle drop and re-drop, stored captures (reload, Open menu, forget), photo close-ups and lightbox, binary USDC with textures, error toasts, blocked storage, snapshot; synthetic capture-bundle fixtures; unit coverage with ratcheting thresholds; sharded CI job. See docs/TESTING.md."],[270,"[x] **iOS JPEG photo export**: write `images/*.jpg` (or a `photos/` folder of 2048 px JPEGs) next to the HEICs in the bundle so Chrome/Firefox skip the 2 MB WASM HEIC decoder and decoding is instant; the web side already prefers whatever decodes natively. Done: `photos/*.jpg` (2048 px, upright) + `manifest.photos`; the web reader uses them when present."],[259,"[x] **Keep captures across reloads**: cache the unzipped model of the last opened bundles in IndexedDB/OPFS (best effort, quota-aware) so a reload reopens a capture scene without re-dropping the `.bikecapture.zip`."],[297,"[x] **Performance**: Draco/Meshopt compression, KTX2 textures, lazy loading, 60 fps on iPhone Safari with 50 pins. Lazily loaded, self-hosted decoders; `tools/optimize-glb.mjs`; BVH picking/occlusion in a worker; budgeted pin updates; device-aware quality (`?quality=low|high`); `tools/bench/` benchmark. See docs/PERFORMANCE.md."],[269,"[x] **Photo close-ups per area**: use `poses.json` to find the capture photos that look most directly at each area target (angle + distance score) and show them as a filmstrip under the area; tap to open full screen. HEIC → JPEG conversion at export time on iOS if browsers can't decode HEIC."],[238,"[x] **PR previews**: publish each open stack PR under `/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (docs + viewer) and link them from the Progress page, so the owner can test a PR before merging it."],[248,"[x] **Reconstruction research**: options for bikes (Object Capture on macOS, COLMAP + OpenMVS, Meshroom, Gaussian splats, cloud APIs, AI image-to-3D), recommendation, photo and video capture protocols, owner decisions (docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md). Vendor prices/terms still to verify against current pages."],[304,"[x] **Render on demand**: only render when the camera, model or pins change (idle stage at 0 fps). Saves phone battery and makes the E2E suite much faster on SwiftShader (today every frame costs ~150–250 ms on CPU)."],[275,"[x] **Shareable read-only link**: `?scene=` URL loads a published scene in Present mode with editing hidden; \"Copy share link\" button. Scenes + models served from `apps/web/public/scenes/<id>/`."],[262,"[x] **USDZ robustness**: three r186 reads binary USDC; `apps/web/src/viewer/usd/` fixes its inline-value decoding, speeds up large meshes ~10×, waits for packed textures and falls back to a `tools/usdz-to-glb.py` hint. Synthetic Object-Capture-like fixtures from `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`."],[305,"[x] **WebKit E2E project**: run the suite in Playwright WebKit (closest to iPhone Safari) on a macOS runner or with WebKit's Linux deps; the `mobile` project is Chromium with an iPhone viewport today."],[264,"[x] **Weld USDZ meshes**: three expands face-varying meshes to 3 vertices per triangle (~3M vertices for a 1M-triangle capture); identical corners are merged into an indexed geometry (hash-based, typed arrays, O(n)): 2.9M → 0.49M vertices, 89 → 26 MB of geometry on the 1M-triangle fixture. Decimation stays offline (`tools/optimize-glb.mjs --simplify`). See docs/PERFORMANCE.md."],[110,"**`apps/ios`**: iPhone capture app (Apple Object Capture: background removed automatically, on-device 3D build, camera poses, shareable bundle)."],[111,"**`apps/web`**: three.js viewer and editor: clear / chroma-green / studio backgrounds, fly-to areas, comment pins, presentation mode, JSON export."],[216,"**4K (3840×2160) at 30 fps**, or 60 fps if the light allows a fast shutter; HEVC or H.264,\n**not** HDR / Dolby Vision (tone mapping varies between decoders); lock exposure and focus;\nstabilization on; no zooming."],[206,"**AI image-to-3D**: never as \"the bike\". Only for placeholders, clearly labeled."],[120,"**Auto-orient on a real capture** (needs the real-capture test below): open a real `.bikecapture.zip`\nand check the bike stands upright, front to the right (+X), drive side towards the default camera.\nIf not, note which button fixed it (Flip / Turn 180° / rotate) so the heuristics can be tuned."],[44,"**Auto-orient** (`apps/web/src/scene/orient.ts`, pure, unit-tested). Target frame: +X front,\n+Y up, +Z drive side, tyres on y = 0. Up to 50k strided vertices (≈3 ms for 1M vertices):"],[26,"**Budget**: LRU by last use, `min(500 MB, 50% of the quota − other usage)` from\n`navigator.storage.estimate()`. A bundle larger than the whole budget is simply not cached."],[208,"**Camera**: any camera ≥ 12 MP; fixed zoom (no zooming between shots); f/8–f/11 for depth of\nfield; ISO as low as possible; shutter ≥ 1/125 s handheld (tripod: anything); lock focus and\nexposure per ring; RAW+JPEG or high-quality JPEG; no portrait mode or beauty filters."],[96,"**Capture → viewer in under 15 minutes** with no desktop software: capture on iPhone,\nAirDrop the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer."],[125,"**Capture guidance + JPEG export on a device** (#14, needs an iPhone with LiDAR): during a capture,\nopen the checklist: each completed orbit ticks the next orbit row and its shot count stays\nfixed after **Another pass**; the top bar counts shots for the current pass only. Export a\nbundle and check (a) export of ~150 photos finishes in reasonable time with the spinner, (b)\n`photos/IMG_*.jpg` are 2048 px on the long edge and **upright** for portrait and landscape\nshots (open a few on the Mac), (c) the zip grew by roughly 0.5 MB per photo, (d) close-ups in\ndesktop Chrome load without the `heic` worker. Note: the iOS app was compile-checked by CI only\n(no Xcode on the agent's Mac); the JPEG writer was verified with ImageIO on macOS."],[122,"**Close-ups on a real capture**: open a real `.bikecapture.zip` with a few areas and check that\neach area's first photos really show it, in Chrome (WASM HEIC path) and iPhone Safari (native)."],[205,"**Cloud API** only after the owner picks a vendor, a budget and accepts its data terms."],[131,"**Cloud API**: use a paid service (KIRI Engine API, Luma, Polycam…)? Which one, monthly budget,\nand are its data terms acceptable for customer bikes? Needs an account and an API key stored as a secret, never in the repo."],[43,"**Crop box** (`crop?: { min, max, enabled }`, model-root space, optional and lenient: a\nmalformed crop is dropped, swapped corners are reordered). The viewer turns it into six world\nclipping planes on the model's own materials (local clipping, shadows clipped too), recomputed only\nwhen the model transform or the box changes. Raycasts skip hits outside the box (no comments on\ncropped-away parts, no occlusion by them), pins outside it are hidden, and exact bounds (framing,\non-ground, auto-orient samples) only count kept vertices. Edit mode shows the box with one handle\nper face (`viewer/cropBox.ts`): pointer events in the capture phase, so mouse and touch drags never\norbit the camera; the face moves along its axis to the point nearest the pointer ray, clipping\nlive, and the store is updated once on release. \"Fit to bike\" (`scene/crop.ts`, pure) samples\npoints along triangle edges, cuts above the floor slab (a dense, wide band in the lower third of\nthe up axis) and keeps the largest 26-connected voxel cluster with a 2% margin. Area-mode captures\nget that box pre-computed but disabled, a hint in the toast, and auto-orient waits until the crop\nis on. Turning the crop on/off or fitting it re-grounds the visible part."],[119,"**Crop on a real area-mode capture**: capture a bike in area mode, open the bundle, turn on\nEdit → Model → Crop and check \"Fit to bike\" removes the floor and the room. Note scans where the\nbike touches a wall or stand (the box then includes it; drag the faces to fix)."],[118,"**Customer link on a real phone**: open the published demo link\n(`…/app/?scene=scenes/demo/scene.bike.json&view=present`) on an iPhone, check swiping, the\nbottom sheet, pin taps and the share sheet. Real customer captures should be published to a\nhost you control with `node tools/publish-scene.mjs <zip> --out <folder>`, not committed here."],[121,"**Decide on the HEIC decoder license**: photo close-ups decode HEIC in Chrome/Firefox with\n`libheif-js` (LGPL-3.0), shipped as a separate, lazily loaded worker chunk. Fine for a private\ntool; before a public release, either confirm LGPL compliance (unmodified library in its own\nfile, notice in the about/credits) or remove it once the iOS app exports JPEGs (see ROADMAP)."],[202,"**Default: Object Capture on a Mac** (`tools/reconstruct/macos/` Swift CLI over an image folder,\nthen package to `bike-capture/1` with `poses.json` from the `.poses` request). It is free, gives the\nbest masked, textured mesh for this object class, and works with photos from any camera and\nwith frames pulled from a video. Detail `.full` for the web (then GLB + decimate), `.raw` only for archiving."],[132,"**Dulling spray**: acceptable on customer bikes, or only polarizer + diffuse light?"],[325,"**Edit**: tap the bike to drop a comment pin; save the current camera as a new area."],[27,"**Failure**: every call is best effort. Any storage error leaves the app as if the cache did\nnot exist; entries whose files vanished (browser eviction) are dropped from the index."],[203,"**Fallback: COLMAP + OpenMVS in Docker** (Linux / CI / a rented GPU box) for when no Mac is\navailable: same `ingest` → `reconstruct` → `package` flow, plus mesh cropping to the bike.\nExpect worse wheels and paint."],[98,"**Fast on phones**: first model visible in < 3 s on iPhone Safari over 4G for a 20 MB model;\n60 fps orbiting with 50 pins."],[126,"**GitHub Pages**: done by the owner on 2026-10-27 (Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch\n`gh-pages`). The site is published from this repo by `tools/publish-pages.sh`."],[40,"**GLB decoders** (`loaders.ts`, `gltfInfo.ts`): `extensionsUsed` decides which of Meshopt, Draco\nand KTX2/Basis is imported; their WASM ships in the build (no CDN)."],[130,"**GPU box**: rent (per-hour cloud GPU) or own an NVIDIA machine for COLMAP dense and Gaussian splats? Budget?"],[25,"**Keys**: one entry per `bundle:` model URL; files live under `cap-<slug>-<fnv1a(url)>/…` and an\n`index.json` lists entries (validated on read). An entry remembers the scene id it was opened\nas, so a different bike exported with the same zip filename never loads the wrong model."],[127,"**Let Actions publish the site** (auto-publish on `develop` and PR previews): Settings →\nActions → General → Workflow permissions → **Read and write permissions**, so the\n`GITHUB_TOKEN` of `pages.yml` and `pr-preview.yml` may push to `gh-pages`. If `gh-pages` has a\nbranch protection rule, allow GitHub Actions to push to it. Check after the first run: the\n\"Publish site\" / \"PR preview\" run is green and Settings → Pages shows a new deployment. PRs\nonly get a preview once their branch contains `pr-preview.yml` (it runs from the PR's own\ncode), so PRs below this one in the stack get theirs after they are rebased or merged."],[97,"**Looks like the real bike**: textures, thin parts (spokes, cables) acceptable; background gone."],[129,"**Mac for the default path**: is an Apple silicon Mac (macOS 14+) available to run Object Capture\n(`PhotogrammetrySession`) on photo folders? Without one, the fallback is COLMAP + OpenMVS on Linux."],[152,"**Meshopt** (default) decodes fastest and has the smallest decoder; **Draco** compresses geometry\nharder but costs a ~190 KB WASM download and slower decoding."],[42,"**Model transform.** The loader wraps the model so its native bounding box is centered on X/Z\nand rests on y = 0 (`centerOnGround`, deterministic per file); that frame is *model-root space*.\n`model.scale`, `model.rotation` (Euler XYZ, three.js convention) and `model.offset` are then\napplied to the root as `world = offset + R · (scale · p)`. Annotations and hotspot views stay in\nmodel-root space, so re-orienting a capture never detaches a comment. The overview camera is\nframed in world space (camera up is world +Y) and converted back."],[204,"**Photoreal later: Gaussian splats** from the same video (COLMAP poses + gsplat/nerfstudio, or\nPolycam/Luma/Scaniverse export) once the viewer loads `.spz`/`.ply` splats."],[61,"**Photos** (`src/ui/photoLibrary.ts`): extracted one at a time from the dropped zip via its\ncentral directory (`src/scene/zipIndex.ts`: the `File` stays on disk, nothing else is inflated),\ndecoded natively (`createImageBitmap`, then `<img>`; Safari reads HEIC), else HEIC goes to a\nmodule worker that lazily loads libheif (`libheif-js`, WASM, ~2 MB, LGPL-3.0, only fetched when a\nHEIC photo is shown). Results are downscaled to JPEG (360 px thumbnails, 2048 px full) and added\nto the capture cache entry, so after a reload the photos already seen still show without the zip."],[39,"**Pins** (`pins.ts`): allocation-free projection against a cached viewport size, transform-only\nwrites for pins that moved, `offscreen` class for pins behind the camera or off the stage,\nocclusion raycasts under a 3 ms per-frame budget that finish on idle animation frames."],[326,"**Present**: steps through the areas one by one, as you would with a customer."],[37,"**Quality** (`quality.ts`): pixel ratio ≤ 2 (1.5 on phones for captures over 400k triangles),\nMSAA only at 1×, smaller hard shadows on phones; `?quality=low|high` overrides."],[60,"**Ranking** (`src/scene/photos.ts`, pure): keep photos whose frustum contains the target\n(assumed iPhone wide camera, 65° × 51°, landscape sensor; poses carry no intrinsics), drop\ncameras behind the surface (`side` hint), score `0.45·centered + 0.35·closeness + 0.2·facing`\n(closeness relative to the nearest usable photo, so units do not matter), and skip near-duplicate\nviewpoints. Occlusion is not tested."],[38,"**Raycasts** (`bvh.ts`): after the first frame of a model, meshes over 5k triangles get a\nthree-mesh-bvh hierarchy (built in `bvh.worker.ts` for big meshes, indirect so the GPU index buffer\nis untouched). `viewer.raycastReady` tells the pins when occlusion tests are cheap."],[124,"**Real iPhone capture test** (needs an iPhone with LiDAR, iOS 18+): build `apps/ios`, capture a\nbike, export the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer. Report whether the USDZ loads."],[123,"**Real Object Capture USDZ in the viewer** (needs a real capture): drop the `model.usdz` (or\nthe `.bikecapture.zip`) on the viewer and compare with Quick Look on the Mac/iPhone: textures\npresent and not flipped, size in meters, bike upright, normal-map bumps not exaggerated. The\nbrowser console logs `USDZ …: N triangles, unzip/parse/build ms`; note those numbers in the\nPR. If anything is off, describe the file structure (`usdcat model.usdz | head -80` without\nsharing the capture) so an agent can re-create it in `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`."],[215,"**Reflective paint**: polarizer on the lens (and ideally on the lights), more diffuse light, or a\nremovable dulling spray if the shop agrees. Record which one you used in the manifest notes."],[36,"**Render on demand** (`renderScheduler.ts`): the animation loop only runs while something changes.\nViewer methods (`setModel`, `setView`, `applyTransform`, `setBackground`, resize, controls input,\nfly-to) call `viewer.requestRender()`; **code that mutates the three.js scene directly must call it\ntoo**. The shadow map is redrawn only on `requestRender()` (scene changes), never for camera-only\nframes. Frame listeners (`onFrame`, pins) run after drawn frames only."],[100,"**Robust**: untrusted files never crash the app; every failure says what to do next."],[99,"**Selling tool, not a 3D toy**: areas and comments are the primary UI; present mode is\nusable by a non-technical salesperson with one hand."],[207,"**Setup**: bike on a stand or a turntable, wheels off the ground or the kickstand hidden; plain\nmatte backdrop that differs from the paint; textured floor or newspaper so the poses solve;\nsoft, even light (two softboxes at 45°, or overcast outdoors), no direct sun, no flash."],[209,"**Shots: 120–200** total, 70–80 % overlap between neighbors:"],[217,"**Shutter speed ≥ 1/250 s** (set it in a pro camera app such as Blackmagic Camera; the stock iOS app\npicks it automatically), otherwise motion blur kills features on spokes and cables."],[218,"**Slow orbit**: about 60–90 s per ring (≈ 4–6°/s), three rings as above, then slow passes over\nthe close-up areas. 3–5 minutes of footage in total."],[59,"**Spaces.** A pose is a column-major camera→reconstruction matrix, camera looking down -Z,\n+Y up. Scene positions are in model-root space. `Viewer.setModel` adds `centerOnGround(object)`\nto the model root, so `modelRoot ⟵ reconstruction` is the loaded object's local matrix (the\ncentering shift plus any root transform the loader applied) times the identity wrapper:\n`src/viewer/captureSpace.ts`. The scene's `model.rotation/scale/offset` sit on the model root\nitself and never enter the mapping. A unit test runs the fixture USDZ through three's\n`USDLoader` + `centerOnGround` and checks the expected close-ups win."],[185,"**Status of the facts below (2026-10-27).** This first pass comes from the author's own knowledge\nof these tools. It was **not** re-checked against vendor pages in this session because the budget\nwas cut short. Prices, limits and terms of cloud services change often: check each `verify:` item\nbefore anyone commits money or customer photos. What was checked in the sandbox: Ubuntu 24.04\nships `colmap 3.9.1` in `universe` (`apt-get install colmap` works, CPU build without CUDA). There\nis no Docker daemon and no GPU here, so OpenMVS and dense reconstruction were not run."],[133,"**Test capture**: shoot one bike with the photo protocol and one 4K video with the video protocol,\nso the pipeline can be measured on real input (keep the files out of the repo)."],[214,"**Turntable vs walk-around**: turntable with a fixed camera is fastest and steadiest, but the\nbackground must stay out of frame or be masked (static background + rotating bike confuses SfM).\nWalk-around works anywhere and is better for the floor features. Object Capture handles both."],[28,"**UI**: \"Open…\" becomes a small menu once something is stored: \"Choose a file…\" plus the stored\ncaptures (name, size, × to forget)."],[324,"**View**: drag to orbit, pinch to zoom, tap an area chip (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit…) to fly there."],[23,"**What**: the model bytes, `manifest.json`, `poses.json` and the image list. Lazily extracted\nfiles (photos, thumbnails) can be added to an entry later (`putFile`) and are evicted with it.\nThe zip itself is not kept (HEIC photos make it hundreds of MB)."],[24,"**Where**: OPFS (`navigator.storage.getDirectory()`, folder `bike-captures/`, flat\npercent-encoded file names), falling back to IndexedDB (`bike-3d-brew` / `files`) when OPFS is\nmissing, has no `createWritable()` (older Safari) or refuses a probe write. Neither → no cache,\nthe old \"drop the zip again\" behavior. `navigator.storage.persist()` is requested once per page\nload, on the first store."],[153,"`--simplify <ratio>` (meshoptimizer's simplifier, `--error` as a fraction of the mesh radius,\ndefault 0.001) is the decimation step for phones: Object Capture's `.full` detail is far more than a\n6\" screen shows."],[154,"`--textures webp|--max-texture` use sharp (installed with glTF Transform). `ktx2` (ETC1S) keeps\ntextures compressed in GPU memory (a 4096² texture: 64 MB as RGBA8, 8–16 MB transcoded to ETC2, ASTC or BC7), the\nbiggest memory win on phones, and needs `toktx` on PATH."],[4,"`bike-capture/1` (iOS export zip)"],[8,"`bike-scene/1` (viewer JSON, `*.bike.json`)"],[9,"`bike-share/1` (share package, `*.bikeshare.zip`) and the customer link"],[383,"`buildFixtures()` returns every fixture as bytes and is also imported by unit tests. Output is\nbyte-for-byte deterministic (fixed zip timestamps, rounded floats), so nothing binary is\ncommitted. What it makes:"],[412,"`capture-cache.spec.ts`: a reload reopens the last capture from OPFS with its comments; the\nOpen menu lists stored captures (most recent first, size, current one marked), switches between\nthem, closes on Esc / outside click, \"Choose a file…\", forgets them; forgotten means a reload\nasks for the zip again. `files.spec.ts` keeps the re-drop flow with capture storage blocked\n(`blockCaptureStorage()`)."],[32,"`composer.ts` (`FastUSDComposer`): typed-array fast path for all-triangle meshes. Stock three took\n~1.4–2.2 s to build a 1M-triangle mesh (JS arrays per index); this takes ~0.2 s, same output."],[31,"`crate.ts` (`CrateParser`): values the crate stores **inline** that r186 misreads: small integral\n`double2/3/4` and `half3/4` (packed int8, e.g. `xformOp:translate = (0, 0, 5)` became a number and\ncrashed the transform), negative `int`, `half`; plus scalar `half3/4`, `quath`, `int4`, `matrix2d/3d`."],[408,"`edit.spec.ts`: add/edit/delete a comment picked on the canvas; persistence across reload;\nCancel/Escape; default area; save/rename/set view/delete areas; bike details."],[414,"`files.spec.ts` also drops the committed binary USDC fixture and checks it renders with its\ndiffuse and normal textures decoded."],[410,"`files.spec.ts`: export JSON → re-import; `?scene=` published scene (routed); capture bundles\nvia picker and drag-and-drop (USDZ, GLB, flat); re-drop after reload restores comments;\nbroken poses warning; bare model drop; error toasts for seven kinds of bad files."],[396,"`main.ts` exposes `window.__bike = { app, store, viewer, ready }` only in the dev server or when\nthe URL has `?e2e` (the suite always adds it). Tests use it to:"],[353,"`make-capture-bundle.mjs`"],[376,"`npm run test:coverage` writes `coverage/` (text summary, HTML report, `coverage-summary.json`).\nThresholds in `apps/web/vite.config.ts` are a ratchet set just under the current numbers,\nglobally and for `src/scene/**`; CI fails when coverage drops below them (and the web job\nprints the totals in its step summary). At the time of writing: lines 99.8%, statements 98.9%,\nfunctions 98%, branches 92.8%. When you raise\ncoverage, raise the thresholds in the same PR. Never lower them to make a PR pass."],[102,"`npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build` and the E2E suite pass; CI green."],[415,"`perf.spec.ts`: an idle stage renders 0 frames, orbiting renders and stops again with pins moved, canvas snapshots work without a preserved drawing buffer, and Meshopt / Draco / KTX2 GLBs (from `tools/fixtures/make-compressed-glb.mjs`) open with self-hosted decoders and no foreign requests."],[199,"`PhotogrammetrySession` takes a folder URL of images from any camera. EXIF focal length helps.\nDepth and gravity metadata (iPhone LiDAR HEIC) improve scale and orientation. Without them the\nscale is arbitrary and the model may come out tilted, so auto-orient (ROADMAP M2) becomes required."],[413,"`photos.spec.ts`: a saved area shows its best photos (all thumbnails decode), the lightbox\nsteps with ←/→ and ‹ › with wrap-around, Esc closes only the lightbox; Present mode shows the\nstrip; after a reload the thumbnails come from browser storage."],[409,"`present.spec.ts`: keys (←, →, space, Esc) and ‹ › buttons with wrap-around; `?mode=present`."],[57,"`src/entry.ts` loads only `present/BikePresenter.ts` for `?view=present`, so customers never\ndownload editing code. The presenter is a self-contained module: `mountPresenter(container,\noptions)` returns a controller with `goToArea`, `next`, `prev`, `play`, `pause`, `setBackground`\nand `on(event)` for `ready`, `error`, `areachange` and `commentopen`. It scopes its CSS under\n`.bike-present` and only takes keys while focused, which is the base for an iframe embed or a\n`<bike-viewer>` element (see ROADMAP)."],[411,"`storage.spec.ts`: everything still works with `localStorage` throwing."],[151,"`tools/optimize-glb.mjs` turns a GLB (for a USDZ capture, first `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`) into a\nphone-friendly one with glTF Transform:"],[56,"`tools/publish-scene.mjs` validates a package (size limits: zip 300 MB, model 250 MB, JSON 2 MB,\n8 MB × 64 photos; JPEG only; no paths outside the package; `parseScene`) and installs it under\n`apps/web/public/scenes/<id>/`. The customer link is\n`…/app/?scene=scenes/<id>/scene.bike.json&view=present` (`kiosk=1&interval=<s>&idle=<s>` for a\nshop screen). Scene, model and photo URLs must be same-origin or https."],[33,"`usdz.ts` (`loadUsd`): unzips only USD layers and images, takes the first layer as root (falls back\nto the first USD layer anywhere), composes, welds the face-varying expansion back into an indexed\nmesh (`../weld.ts`: 2.9M → 0.49M vertices for 1M triangles), waits for textures (blob URLs created and revoked by\nthree per image), halves three's normal-map strength for the standard scale 2 / bias -1 decode,\nand reports undecodable textures as warnings instead of failing."],[407,"`view.spec.ts`: demo loads with seeded areas/comments/pins and no console errors; fly to an\narea and back; comment focus; background modes (and the chroma-green opaque clear); Snapshot\ndownloads a real PNG; Reset view."],[12,"`wesbos/3d-model-anything` records RoomPlan + LiDAR mesh + posed photos, then an AI agent\nrebuilds the room in three.js. A bike is one object with thin tubes, spokes and cables, so we\nuse Apple's Object Capture: guided orbits, **automatic object masking** (the background is\nremoved during reconstruction; no green screen needed) and a textured USDZ. We keep Wes's\nkey idea of **posed photos**: `poses.json` tells us where each photo was taken, so the viewer\ncan show real close-up photos for an area (e.g. the fork crown) next to the 3D view."],[183,"> \"We can have the best 3D experience, but if it doesn't come from a collection of photos and\n> videos of a bike, it's not useful.\" (owner)"],[144,"| Area                        | What                                                                                                                                                         | Where    |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------- |\n| No preserved drawing buffer | The canvas keeps its last frame while idle anyway; `screenshot()` renders right before reading. Saves a full-screen copy per frame on tile-based phone GPUs. | `Viewer` |"],[149,"| Area                       | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | Where                                     |\n| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Lazy, self-hosted decoders | A GLB's `extensionsUsed` decides which decoder is imported: Meshopt (~26 KB JS with inline WASM), Draco (glTF build, ~190 KB WASM, workers), KTX2/Basis (~530 KB WASM, workers). three's loaders resolve the files with `new URL(…, import.meta.url)`, so Vite ships them in `dist/assets/`; nothing comes from a CDN. Plain GLBs fetch none. | `viewer/loaders.ts`, `viewer/gltfInfo.ts` |"],[145,"| Area                 | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | Where               |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------- |\n| Device-aware quality | Pixel ratio ≤ 2 (phones show no gain at 3×, which shades 2.25× the pixels), 1.5 on phones for captures over 400k triangles; MSAA only at 1× (2× already supersamples); 1024² hard shadows on phones, 2048² soft on desktop. `?quality=low` (1×, 512² shadows) and `?quality=high` (up to 3×, MSAA) override. | `viewer/quality.ts` |"],[146,"| Area               | What                                                                                                                                                                                 | Where                           |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------- |\n| Welded USDZ meshes | three expands face-varying primvars to three vertices per triangle; identical corners are merged back into an indexed mesh (O(n) open-addressing hash over typed arrays, bit-exact). | `viewer/weld.ts`, `usd/usdz.ts` |"],[142,"| Area             | What                                                                                                                                                                                                  | Where                                                 |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Render on demand | The animation loop runs only while something changes (controls input and damping, a fly-to, a model / background / pin / size change). An idle stage draws **0 frames**; a hidden tab stops the loop. | `viewer/renderScheduler.ts`, `Viewer.requestRender()` |"],[143,"| Area           | What                                                                                                                                                                                         | Where                                     |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Cached shadows | The sun and the model stand still while the camera orbits, so the shadow map is redrawn only when the scene changes, not for camera frames (that pass re-draws every triangle of the model). | `Viewer` (`shadowMap.autoUpdate = false`) |"],[147,"| Area         | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Where                                          |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| BVH raycasts | After the first frame of a model, meshes over 5k triangles get a three-mesh-bvh hierarchy, built in a worker for big meshes (copies, never transfers, so the geometry stays usable; indirect, so the GPU index buffer is untouched). Picking and pin occlusion use it. | `viewer/bvh.ts`, `bvhImpl.ts`, `bvh.worker.ts` |"],[148,"| Area | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | Where            |\n| ---- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| Pins | Projection into a scratch object against a cached viewport size (no layout reads), transform-only writes for pins that moved, an `offscreen` class for pins behind the camera or off the stage, occlusion raycasts under a 3 ms per-frame budget that continue on idle animation frames (without re-rendering) until every visible pin is current. Skipped until the BVH exists for big models. | `viewer/pins.ts` |"],[387,"| File                                | What it exercises                          |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `bike-broken-poses.bikecapture.zip` | invalid `poses.json`: opens with a warning |"],[388,"| File                            | What it exercises                  |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `bike-no-model.bikecapture.zip` | capture never reconstructed: error |"],[386,"| File                        | What it exercises                    |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `bike-flat.bikecapture.zip` | flat zip with Finder `__MACOSX` junk |"],[389,"| File                        | What it exercises              |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `not-a-zip.bikecapture.zip` | text with a `.zip` name: error |"],[385,"| File                       | What it exercises                                                |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike-glb.bikecapture.zip` | same bike as GLB (three's `GLTFExporter` in Node, vertex colors) |"],[390,"| File                    | What it exercises |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `bike.usdz`, `bike.glb` | bare model files  |"],[374,"| File                    | Why it cannot run in Node         |\n| ----------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `src/ui/heic.worker.ts` | a Web Worker running libheif WASM |"],[384,"| File                   | What it exercises                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike.bikecapture.zip` | iOS layout (everything under one folder): manifest, ASCII-USD `model.usdz` of a low-poly vertex-colored bike (wheels, frame tubes, fork, cockpit, saddle, drivetrain as named meshes), `poses.json` with 32 cameras on three rings looking at the bike, 32 tiny placeholder PNG photos, `record.json` |"],[373,"| File                   | Why it cannot run in Node                          |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/viewer/Viewer.ts` | `WebGLRenderer`, `OrbitControls`, `ResizeObserver` |"],[372,"| File            | Why it cannot run in Node                |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `src/ui/app.ts` | UI controller driving the WebGL `Viewer` |"],[375,"| File            | Why it cannot run in Node |\n| --------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `src/**/*.d.ts` | type declarations only    |"],[371,"| File          | Why it cannot run in Node                |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `src/main.ts` | page bootstrap: the whole DOM plus WebGL |"],[379,"| Generator                                                 | Output                                                                                                          | Used by                                                                                                            |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-capture.mjs` (+ `render-photos.mjs`) | a USDZ bundle off-origin like a real reconstruction, orbit + close-up poses, placeholder or **rendered** photos | `photos.test.ts`, `capture.test.ts`, E2E photo close-ups (`bike-photos.bikecapture.zip`), `npm run fixture:photos` |"],[378,"| Generator                                | Output   