s/`, same file stems, ≤ 2048 px long edge, EXIF orientation baked into the pixels (orientation 1). Listed as `manifest.photos` |"],[17,"| Path      | Content                                           |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `images/` | Object Capture HEIC photos (reconstruction input) |"],[343,"| PR                                     | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #14 iOS capture guidance + JPEG photos | On the iPhone: during a capture tap **Checklist**: orbits tick themselves after each completed pass, close-ups tick on tap, the top bar shows shots for the current pass. Export a bundle: the zip has `photos/*.jpg` next to `images/*.HEIC` and `manifest.json` has `\"photos\": \"photos/\"`. Open it in desktop Chrome: close-up photos appear without the HEIC decoder (no `heic` worker request in DevTools → Network). Web side alone: `npm test` (capture.test.ts covers the `photos/` preference). |"],[345,"| PR                             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #15 Auto-publish + PR previews | Open the home page: **PR previews** lists open PRs with Viewer and Docs links; open `/bike-3d-brew/pr/15/app/` and the demo bike loads. Push to a PR and its preview updates a few minutes later (Actions → \"PR preview\"); close it and it disappears from the list. Merging into `develop` updates the main site (Actions → \"Publish site\"). |"],[346,"| PR                             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #17 Site follows the stack tip | The home page has no credits box any more. Push to the top PR of the stack (or press *Run workflow* on Actions → \"Publish site\" from it): the main site shows that branch a few minutes later (the footer names it). Pushes to other branches skip publishing. |"],[336,"| PR                       | What to try                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #2 Capture bundle import | **Open…** the synthetic bundle above (or drop it on desktop): it loads and is named from the manifest. Add a comment, reload, open the same file again: the comment is back. |"],[341,"| PR                      | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #8 Share with customers | Open the published demo as a customer: `/bike-3d-brew/app/?scene=scenes/demo/scene.bike.json&view=present` (on your phone too). Swipe between areas, tap a pin (leader line to its card), add `&kiosk=1&interval=4` for auto-play that pauses when you touch it. In the editor, **Share** on a published scene copies the link; on a local capture it exports a `.bikeshare.zip` that `node tools/publish-scene.mjs <zip>` installs. In Edit mode, drag comments to reorder them and use **bold**, *italic* and `- ` lists in bodies. |"],[342,"| PR              | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #12 Performance | Orbit the demo, then let go: the camera glides to a stop and the page goes quiet (DevTools → Performance shows no frames while idle). Pins slide with the bike and dim when the bike is in front of them. On a phone, open a large capture: it appears, then picking a comment point is instant. Add `?quality=low` to the URL for the cheapest rendering. A GLB made with `node tools/optimize-glb.mjs in.glb out.glb` opens like any other. |"],[339,"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #9 Auto-orient | Make a tilted bundle (`node tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs --out tilted.bikecapture.zip`) and **Open…** it: the bike stands up facing right and the toast says \"Auto-oriented\". In **Edit → Model** try Undo (back to lying on its side), Auto-orient, the rotate ±90° buttons, Turn 180°, and type a real length in cm. Pin a comment first: it stays on the same spot through every rotation. |"],[338,"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #7 Test system | Nothing new to click: `npm run e2e` drives the real viewer through every flow above (demo, edit, present, export/import, capture bundles, stored captures, photo close-ups, error toasts) at desktop and iPhone sizes; `npm run test:coverage` shows unit coverage. The suite found and fixed a bug where a tap right after jumping to an area (with reduced motion on) missed the bike. |"],[344,"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #16 WebKit E2E | Nothing new to click. On a Mac: `npx playwright install webkit && npm run e2e:webkit` runs the iPhone flows in Safari's engine (45 tests). Open the customer link in Safari on your phone: no console error when the Present card changes height. |"],[335,"| PR            | What to try                                                                           |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #1 Foundation | Demo bike, areas, comments, Edit and Present modes, background switcher, Export JSON. |"],[340,"| PR           | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #10 Crop box | Make an area-mode bundle with a floor and clutter (`node tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs --out area.bikecapture.zip --rotate 0,0,0 --offset 0,0,0 --ground --mode area`) and **Open…** it: the toast suggests cropping. In **Edit → Model → Crop** turn the crop on, press **Fit to bike** (floor and crate disappear), then drag a face handle with the mouse or a finger: the camera must not orbit while dragging. Comments can't be pinned on cropped-away parts, and pins outside the box hide. |"],[337,"| PR        | What to try                                                                     |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docs site | This site: the home page shows roadmap progress; **Progress** lists every item. |"],[186,"| Property                                 | Effect on photogrammetry                                                                                                  | Mitigation                                                                                                                  |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Thin parts (spokes ~2 mm, cables, chain) | Few pixels wide, so few features. Dense MVS fills them in or drops them. Meshes come out with webbed wheels or no spokes. | Close passes at the wheels; accept \"disc\" wheels or model spokes procedurally later; splats handle them better than meshes. |"],[187,"| Property                        | Effect on photogrammetry                                                                       | Mitigation                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Glossy / metallic paint, chrome | Highlights move with the viewpoint, which breaks feature matching and creates holes and bumps. | Diffuse, overcast-like light (softboxes, cloudy day, shade); polarizer; dulling / 3D-scanning spray (AESUB Blue vanishes in about 4 h) on matte-safe parts only, never without the shop's OK. |"],[189,"| Property                        | Effect on photogrammetry                               | Mitigation                                                                               |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Size ~1.7 × 1 m, open structure | Background visible through the frame; masking matters. | Plain backdrop or a turntable; object masking (Object Capture does it, COLMAP does not). |"],[188,"| Property                  | Effect on photogrammetry      | Mitigation                                                               |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Black tyres, black carbon | Low texture, so few features. | More light; textured backdrop and floor so the camera poses still solve. |"],[190,"| Property        | Effect on photogrammetry                       | Mitigation                                                    |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Symmetric sides | Matching can confuse the left and right sides. | Overlapping rings, top-down ring, markers/props on the floor. |"],[63,"~~Does three.js read Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC)?~~ Yes, with the fixes above, verified on\nsynthetic Object-Capture-like files. Still to confirm on a real capture (docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md)."],[95,"A bike shop captures a bike with an iPhone in a few minutes and gets a background-free,\nphotoreal 3D model that sales staff (in store, on a tablet) and customers (on a shared link)\ncan spin, zoom into named areas (fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and read pinned sales comments."],[321,"A short guide for the owner: how to try what the agents built, on a phone or a laptop. Every\nPR that adds something testable extends the \"What each PR adds\" table at the bottom."],[394,"A third project, `webkit`, runs the iPhone 14 profile in Playwright's WebKit (the engine of iPhone\nSafari) over the view, edit, present, photos, share and files specs. It is opt-in\n(`npm run e2e:webkit`, after `npx playwright install webkit`; the global setup also needs Chromium, which renders the photo fixtures) and local-only for now: on GitHub's\nGPU-less macOS runners every WebKit page load timed out (WebGL), see ROADMAP. It found two\nSafari-only issues: a \"ResizeObserver loop\" page error from the Present card's height update\n(now applied on the next frame), and test contexts without OPFS, where captures use the\nIndexedDB fallback."],[68,"Added"],[311,"AR \"place the bike in your room\" via Quick Look (`model.usdz` + `<a rel=\"ar\">`)."],[1,"Architecture"],[243,"Areas (hotspots) and sales comments pinned to the model surface, edit + present modes"],[79,"Auto-orient captures: a scanned bike is stood upright facing +X (PCA + side-view ground line, bike-shaped sign heuristics) on first load, with a toast; Edit → Model has Auto-orient, rotate ±90° per axis, flip, turn 180°, scale, real length in cm, 1 cm nudges, on-ground, undo and reset. Comments stay attached. `tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs` generates tilted test bundles. (#9)"],[74,"Auto-publish: every push to `develop` republishes the site (`.github/workflows/pages.yml`), and each open PR from this repo gets a preview at `/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (docs + viewer), removed when the PR closes (`pr-preview.yml`), listed under \"PR previews\" on the home and Progress pages from `/pr/index.json`. `tools/publish-pages.sh` gains `--pr`, `--title` and `--remove-pr`, only replaces its own part of gh-pages (the main site keeps `/pr/`), and retries on the latest gh-pages when another run pushed first. (#15)"],[64,"Bike size vs. Object Capture's bounding box limits: area mode is the fallback."],[395,"Browser: CI runs `npx playwright install --with-deps --only-shell chromium`. On a machine with a\npreinstalled Chromium (e.g. the agent containers: `/opt/pw-browsers/chromium`), do not run\n`playwright install`; set `PW_CHROMIUM_PATH=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium` and the config uses it as\n`launchOptions.executablePath`. `@playwright/test` is pinned to the version whose browsers are\npreinstalled there."],[402,"Camera flights are instant because the suite emulates `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, which\nthe viewer honors; a test that wants the animation calls\n`page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion: 'no-preference' })` and waits for `viewer.flying === false`."],[109,"Capture bikes with an iPhone, show them as background-free 3D models, zoom into components\n(fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and pin sales comments on them."],[85,"Capture bundle import: drop an iPhone `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer; it is unzipped in the browser, the model loads and the scene is named from the manifest. Re-dropping a bundle restores its comments. (#2)"],[5,"Capture cache (browser storage)"],[179,"Capture protocol (photos)"],[180,"Capture protocol (video)"],[82,"Captures survive reloads: opened `*.bikecapture.zip` bundles are kept in browser storage (OPFS, IndexedDB fallback, LRU under a quota-aware budget) and reopen automatically; \"Open…\" lists stored captures with size and a forget button. Synthetic fixture generator in `tools/fixtures/`. (#5)"],[66,"Changelog"],[330,"Checks the agents run on every PR (CI runs them too):"],[157,"Chromium + SwiftShader, 1280×800 at 1×, on a shared 4-core container under heavy load (other jobs\nrunning): treat absolute times as noisy, compare before/after. `tools/bench/bench.mjs --model big.usdz`\n(synthetic 23 MB USDZ, 972k triangles, 2048² textures), base branch vs. this change:"],[246,"CI: web typecheck/test/build, unsigned iOS build on macOS, Pages deploy workflow"],[213,"Close-ups (0.4–0.6 m), 4–6 shots each, overlapping each other: drivetrain (both sides of the\nrear derailleur, chainring), fork crown and dropouts, cockpit (bar, stem, shifters), saddle and\nseat clamp, each wheel hub and a sector of spokes from both sides."],[200,"COLMAP poses are world→camera with OpenCV axes (+X right, +Y down, +Z forward). The viewer\nwants camera→model with camera looking down -Z, +Y up. So:\n`T_c2w = inverse([R|t]) = [Rᵀ | -Rᵀt]`, then flip the camera's Y and Z axes:\n`pose = T_c2w · diag(1, -1, -1, 1)`. COLMAP quaternions are `QW QX QY QZ` (Hamilton,\nworld→camera)."],[312,"Compare two bikes side by side."],[3,"Contracts"],[351,"Coverage"],[78,"Crop box: Edit → Model → Crop clips everything outside an axis-aligned box (model-root space, saved as optional `crop` in `bike-scene/1`) with renderer clipping planes; drag the face handles (mouse or touch) or type the corners; \"Fit to bike\" removes the floor slab and background clusters. Cropped-away geometry can't take comments, and comments outside the box are hidden. Area-mode captures get a suggested box and a hint. (#10)"],[87,"Customer link and Present mode in Safari: the card-height update no longer triggers a \"ResizeObserver loop\" page error. (#16)"],[35,"Details and measurements: PERFORMANCE.md."],[104,"Docs (ROADMAP, CHANGELOG, ARCHITECTURE, guides) updated in the same PR."],[83,"Docs & progress site (Fumadocs, `apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown: home dashboard with roadmap progress per milestone, latest changes and build commit; \"How to test\" guide; offline search. `tools/publish-pages.sh` publishes it with the viewer (under `/app/`) and a synthetic test bundle to the `gh-pages` branch; `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` writes a synthetic `*.bikecapture.zip`. The Actions-based `pages.yml` deploy is removed. (#4)"],[62,"Does `PhotogrammetrySession.Poses` return camera→model transforms in the same frame as the\nUSDZ? (Assumed, and the photo close-ups depend on it; validate by checking that an area's top\nclose-up really shows that area on a real capture.)"],[366,"DOM code (`ui/dom.ts`, `viewer/pins.ts`, `ui/photoViewer.ts`, `ui/photoLibrary.ts`,\n`ui/photoDecode.ts`) opts into happy-dom with a first-line comment\n`// @vitest-environment happy-dom`. Browser APIs happy-dom lacks are stubbed per test:\n`createImageBitmap`, `<img>.decode`, `OffscreenCanvas`, `Worker` (photoDecode), pointer capture\n(lightbox gestures), a fake `Viewer` (pins). Decoding itself is mocked in `photoLibrary.test.ts`."],[112,"Drop a `.bikecapture.zip` from the iPhone app (or a `.glb`, `.usdz`, `.ply`) onto the viewer to use your own capture. Switch to **Edit** to\ntap the bike and add comments, save camera views as areas; **Present** steps through areas for\na customer."],[355,"End-to-end tests"],[70,"Every PR adds a line under **Unreleased** (newest first) with its PR number. When the owner\nmerges the stack to `main`, the Unreleased block becomes a dated release."],[400,"Everything else goes through the real UI: clicks, taps, keys, the file picker\n(`setInputFiles`), real `DragEvent` drops with a `DataTransfer`, dialogs and downloads. Keep the\nhook read-mostly; if a test needs to mutate app state through it, that is a sign a UI path is\nmissing."],[370,"Excluded from coverage in `apps/web/vite.config.ts`, each covered by the E2E suite instead:"],[13,"Fallbacks when Object Capture struggles with a bike (thin spokes are the classic failure):\narea mode + a crop box, or a gaussian splat (Scaniverse/Polycam/Luma) for photoreal paint.\nThe green background mode exists for compositing snapshots/videos in other tools."],[398,"find a point on the model to tap: `modelPoint()` in `e2e/helpers.ts` asks the app's own\n`viewer.pick()` and checks `document.elementFromPoint` so the tap lands on the canvas, not a pin;"],[69,"Fixed"],[352,"Fixtures"],[363,"Fixtures for both come from one generator: `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`."],[382,"Folding the three JS generators into one is a ROADMAP follow-up."],[221,"For a dense textured mesh use OpenMVS (`InterfaceCOLMAP` → `DensifyPointCloud` → `ReconstructMesh`\n→ `RefineMesh` → `TextureMesh`) from its Docker image, or COLMAP's dense steps on a CUDA machine."],[58,"For the active area (its view target, preferring cameras on the side its saved view looks from),\nthe active comment (its pin, preferring cameras in front of its surface normal) and each Present\nstep, the viewer shows a filmstrip of the capture photos that best show that point; tapping one\nopens a full-screen viewer (arrows / swipe, pinch / wheel / double-tap zoom, Esc)."],[86,"Foundation: three.js viewer/editor with areas, pinned sales comments, present mode, background modes, `bike-scene/1` format; iOS Object Capture app skeleton; CI. (#1)"],[377,"Four generators, each with a job. All output is synthetic; no real capture is ever committed."],[49,"Front sign: the wide handlebar sits ahead of centre (plus a small vote for the drivetrain mass\nbehind it). Drive side follows from the right-handed frame."],[184,"Goal: **any photo set or video of a bike (any camera) → a `bike-capture/1` bundle the viewer\nopens**: a model (GLB preferred), `poses.json`, `images/` and `manifest.json`. Today the only\nproducer is the iOS Object Capture app."],[90,"Goals"],[47,"Ground line: the longest downward-facing edge of the side-view convex hull (tangent across\nboth tyres) fixes the 5–15° tilt PCA leaves."],[331,"How the automated tests work and how to add them: Testing."],[316,"How to test"],[233,"Ideas parking lot"],[20,"Importing in the browser (`apps/web/src/scene/capture.ts`): dropping a `*.bikecapture.zip`\nunzips it in memory with fflate; nothing is uploaded. The iOS exporter zips its staging folder\n(`NSFileCoordinator .forUploading`), so files usually sit under one top-level directory: the\nshallowest `manifest.json` defines the bundle root and `__MACOSX/` / `._*` entries are ignored.\nOnly `manifest.json`, the model and `poses.json` are decompressed (size-capped); images are just\nlisted; when `manifest.photos` names a non-empty folder, its JPEGs are used instead of the HEICs\n(pose `file` names like `IMG_0007.HEIC` match `IMG_0007.jpg` by stem), so no browser needs the\nWASM HEIC decoder. If `manifest.model` is missing, a `glb`/`gltf`/`usdz`/`ply` next to the manifest is used\n(GLB first, e.g. after `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`). A broken `poses.json` is a warning, not an error."],[245,"iOS app skeleton: Object Capture (object + area mode), on-device reconstruction, poses, bundle export"],[72,"iOS capture guidance + JPEG photos: the capture screen has a checklist (3 orbits at hub height, saddle height and top-down, ticked as Object Capture completes each pass; close-ups of fork crown, dropouts, rear derailleur and cockpit; shots per pass; reflective-paint tips, and why a turntable does not work with on-device Object Capture). Exported bundles add `photos/*.jpg` (2048 px, upright) listed as `manifest.photos`, and the web viewer uses them instead of decoding HEIC. (#14)"],[50,"It runs once when a scene is opened with a non-demo model, no comments and no `model.rotation`\n(`shouldAutoOrient`); the offset is then recomputed from exact bounds so the bike stands on the\nground. Edit → Model exposes the result plus manual rotate/flip/scale/nudge, each one store\nupdate with a small undo stack. Generate tilted test bundles with\n`node tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs --rotate 70,25,-40` (ASCII USD mesh in `model.usdz`)."],[333,"It writes a low-poly bike as `model.glb`, a `manifest.json`, an orbit of camera poses in\n`poses.json` and no photos, all nested in one folder like the real export. Drag the file onto\nthe viewer (or use **Open…**). Dropping the same file again later restores the comments you\nadded to it."],[140,"Known gaps"],[319,"Make a synthetic capture bundle"],[115,"Manual steps"],[235,"Markers: `[ ]` open · `[~]` in progress (draft PR open) · `[x]` done (in an open or merged PR)."],[314,"Measure tool (tap two points → distance in mm)."],[34,"Measured on a synthetic 23 MB USDZ (972k triangles, 2048² texture; `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py\n--detail 90 --tex 2048`), Chromium: unzip 16 ms, parse 183 ms, build 206 ms, textures 24 ms. Parsing\nstays on the main thread: a worker would save the ~0.2 s parse but pay ~0.07 s structured-clone of\nthe spec table back, and the build step needs three.js objects on the main thread anyway. The USD\ncode (~70 KB min) is a lazy chunk loaded on the first USDZ. Anything that still fails shows an error\npointing to `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`. Fixtures are synthetic (`apps/web/test/fixtures/README.md`)."],[138,"Measuring"],[225,"Milestone 0: Project ops"],[226,"Milestone 1: Foundation (PR 1)"],[227,"Milestone 1.5: Photos & video → 3D"],[228,"Milestone 2: Real captures into the viewer"],[229,"Milestone 3: Sales experience"],[230,"Milestone 4: iOS app depth"],[231,"Milestone 5: Backend & multi-bike catalog"],[232,"Milestone 6: Quality"],[401,"Never `waitForTimeout`. Wait on app state (`waitForFunction`, `expect.poll`) or on web-first\nassertions (`toHaveText`, `toHaveCount`, `toHaveAttribute`)."],[170,"No runtime decimation: phones get the full capture unless it went through `optimize-glb --simplify`."],[94,"Non-goals (for now)"],[168,"Not yet measured on a real iPhone (ROADMAP: \"Measure on a real iPhone\")."],[197,"Notes:"],[198,"Object Capture is the only option with **automatic object masking** built in, which matters for\nthe \"background-free\" goal. With COLMAP the bundle needs masking (rembg / U²-Net on the\nphotos before MVS, or cropping the mesh to the dominant cluster after)."],[48,"Object Capture output is gravity-aligned, so if that up is within 6° of ±Y, Y is kept exactly\nand only yaw changes (horizontal PCA)."],[29,"Object Capture writes a USDZ whose root layer is **binary USDC (crate)**: one baked triangle\nmesh, indexed face-varying `primvars:st` and normals, a `UsdPreviewSurface` fed by\n`UsdUVTexture` PNGs in `0/` (diffuse, normal with scale 2 / bias -1, occlusion),\n`metersPerUnit = 1`, `upAxis = \"Y\"`."],[318,"On a laptop"],[406,"On CI a failing run uploads `playwright-report/` and `test-results/` (traces, screenshots) as\nthe `playwright-report` artifact. CI retries once; a test that only passes on retry is reported\nas flaky and should be fixed, not ignored."],[317,"On your phone (no setup)"],[11,"Open questions (verify on device)"],[322,"Open the live demo: **https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/**\n(this site lives one level up: https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/)."],[137,"Optimizing a capture"],[177,"Options"],[108,"Overview"],[182,"Owner decisions"],[128,"Owner decisions for turning any photo set or video into a model (details in RECONSTRUCTION.md):"],[169,"Parsing and welding a big USDZ still run on the main thread (~1 s together for 1M triangles on a\ndesktop CPU, more on a phone); ROADMAP \"Progressive capture loading\"."],[45,"PCA: smallest-variance axis = the bike's width, middle axis = candidate up."],[135,"Performance"],[75,"Performance: the viewer renders on demand (an idle stage draws 0 frames, the loop pauses in hidden tabs), redraws the shadow map only when the scene changes, caps the pixel ratio per device (`?quality=low|high`), welds USDZ meshes into indexed geometry (2.9M → 0.49M vertices on a 1M-triangle capture), builds a BVH in a worker so picking and pin occlusion cost ~0.05 ms instead of ~200 ms, and updates 50+ pins with budgeted occlusion and transform-only writes. GLBs with Meshopt, Draco or KTX2 load with lazily fetched, self-hosted decoders; `tools/optimize-glb.mjs` makes phone-friendly GLBs; `tools/bench/bench.mjs` measures it all. See `docs/PERFORMANCE.md`. (#12)"],[10,"Photo close-ups"],[81,"Photo close-ups: for the active area, the active comment and each Present step, a filmstrip of the capture photos that best show it (ranked from `poses.json`), with a full-screen viewer (swipe, arrows, pinch/zoom). Photos are read lazily from the zip, HEIC is decoded natively or by a lazily loaded WASM worker, and thumbnails are kept in the capture cache. (#6)"],[116,"Photos & video → 3D"],[76,"Photos & video → 3D research (`docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md`): reconstruction options for bikes, recommendation (Object Capture on macOS by default, COLMAP + OpenMVS as fallback, splats later), photo and video capture protocols, owner decisions; new ROADMAP Milestone 1.5. (#11)"],[175,"Photos & video → 3D: reconstruction options for bikes"],[181,"Pipeline (planned shape: `tools/reconstruct/`)"],[393,"Playwright drives the **production build** (`vite build` + `vite preview` on port 4190, started\nby the config's `webServer`) in two projects: `desktop` (1280×800, every spec) and `mobile`\n(iPhone 14 viewport with touch, DPR 1 to keep CPU rendering fast; only the specs where layout and\ntouch matter: view, edit, present, photos). WebGL runs on SwiftShader\n(`--use-angle=swiftshader --enable-unsafe-swiftshader`), so no GPU is needed. CI splits the\nsuite into two parallel shards (`--shard=1/2`, `2/2`)."],[244,"Procedural demo bike with seeded areas and comments"],[91,"Product"],[173,"Progress"],[105,"Public release / app store distribution (the owner decides when)."],[101,"Pure logic in `apps/web/src/scene/` with unit tests; coverage does not go down."],[364,"Pure logic lives in `apps/web/src/scene/` (scene format, store, camera math, capture bundles,\nUI helpers in `helpers.ts`) and is tested in plain Node. When UI code grows a decision (a\ndefault, a message, a URL rule), move it into `src/scene/helpers.ts` and test it there."],[93,"Quality bar for every PR"],[399,"read the scene for assertions (`store.scene`)."],[106,"Real customer captures in the repo: only generated fixtures."],[178,"Recommendation"],[354,"Rendered-photo bundle"],[7,"Rendering and performance (`apps/web/src/viewer/`)"],[139,"Results"],[210,"Ring 1, hub height (~0.35 m), distance ~1.5–2 m: 36–48 shots (every 7.5–10°)."],[211,"Ring 2, saddle height (~0.9 m), looking slightly down: 36–48 shots."],[212,"Ring 3, high (~1.6 m), looking down at 45°: 24–36 shots."],[224,"Roadmap"],[174,"Roadmap status per milestone, generated from ROADMAP.md at build time."],[150,"Rule for new code: anything that changes what the canvas shows outside the `Viewer` methods\n(a new scene object, a material tweak, clipping planes) must call `viewer.requestRender()`, or the\nchange appears only on the next camera move."],[242,"Scene format `bike-scene/1` with validation, local persistence, import/export"],[404,"Screenshots are for humans: `snap(page, testInfo, name)` saves to `test-results/` and attaches\nto the HTML report. Do not add pixel-diff assertions; SwiftShader output differs across\nmachines."],[41,"See `apps/web/src/scene/schema.ts`. A scene references its model by URL (relative to the\nscene file), lists **hotspots** (named camera views: the zoomable areas) and **annotations**\n(surface point + normal, title, body, kind `feature|spec|upgrade|note`, optional price and area).\nAll coordinates are in model-root space."],[113,"See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, ROADMAP.md and\napps/ios/README.md. Inspired by\nwesbos/3d-model-anything."],[222,"See MANUAL-STEPS.md. In short: a Mac (Apple silicon) for the default path;\nwhether to pay for a cloud API (which vendor, monthly budget, OK with its data terms for\ncustomer bikes); a GPU box (rented or owned) for COLMAP dense / splats; whether dulling spray is\nacceptable on customer bikes."],[51,"Share → \"Export share package\" turns a local capture into a self-contained zip\n(`apps/web/src/scene/share.ts`):"],[77,"Share with customers: read-only `?scene=…&view=present` link served by a standalone presenter (`present/BikePresenter.ts`, no editing code, container-scoped), Share button (share sheet / clipboard / visible link), `bike-share/1` package export + `tools/publish-scene.mjs`, published demo at `scenes/demo/`. Present mode: leader lines, progress dots, swipe, auto-play (`?kiosk=1`), phone bottom sheet; markdown-lite comment bodies (DOM-only renderer); drag / ↑↓ comment reordering. (#8)"],[71,"Site follows the stack tip: `pages.yml` republishes whenever the newest ready PR at the top of the stack (or `develop` when none is open) is pushed, so the live site no longer waits for merges. Parallel agents work in `.claude/worktrees/` with their own E2E port; the suite no longer reuses a server it did not start. The session-credits counter is gone from the home page. (#17)"],[313,"Size guide overlay (rider silhouette to scale)."],[22,"So a capture scene survives a reload, every successfully opened bundle is kept in the browser\n(`apps/web/src/scene/captureCache.ts`, pure logic; `apps/web/src/storage/backends.ts`, storage):"],[201,"Splats need a viewer path (Spark / `@sparkjsdev/spark`) and a crop box; pins and areas still work\nbecause they only need a surface to raycast against (a proxy mesh or splat-depth picking)."],[220,"Status and the next steps are in ROADMAP.md (Milestone 1.5). For the commands to try\nCOLMAP on Linux today (a CPU-only sparse model, enough to check the poses):"],[367,"Storage: `storage/backends.ts` runs against `fake-indexeddb` and a small in-memory OPFS\n(`FakeDir` in `backends.test.ts`); `navigator` is replaced with `vi.stubGlobal`."],[92,"Success criteria"],[156,"SwiftShader renders on the CPU, so absolute numbers are far from a phone GPU and swing with machine\nload: compare runs made back to back on the same machine, and read render counts and per-operation\ncosts rather than fps."],[141,"Targets (from GOALS.md): first model visible in **< 3 s** on iPhone Safari over 4G for a\n20 MB model, **60 fps** orbiting with **50 pins**, and **low battery use when idle**."],[80,"Test system: Playwright E2E suite (`npm run e2e`, desktop + iPhone viewport, sharded CI job) over the production build, covering every viewer flow including stored captures, photo close-ups and binary USDC; synthetic capture-bundle fixtures (`tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`, rendered-photo bundle via `render-photos.mjs`); unit coverage with ratcheting thresholds (`npm run test:coverage`, ~99.8% lines) incl. zip64 parsing, OPFS/IndexedDB backends and the photo UI; `docs/TESTING.md`. UI decisions moved into tested `scene/helpers.ts`; `?e2e` test hook. Fixed: a tap right after an instant (reduced-motion) fly-to missed the model. (#7)"],[348,"Testing"],[405,"Tests run in parallel across fresh browser contexts, so each test starts from an empty\n`localStorage` and the seeded demo."],[219,"The `ingest` step extracts frames, keeps the sharpest frame per short time window (variance of the\nLaplacian) and only adds a frame when the view has changed enough, aiming for 80–200 frames."],[356,"The `window.__bike` test hook"],[88,"The active comment pin (and the draft pin) drifted away from its point by 25% of its screen position because CSS `scale` also scaled the position transform. (#9)"],[327,"The background buttons switch between clear, chroma green, studio and dark."],[234,"The backlog autonomous sessions work through, top to bottom. Each item is sized for one\nsession / one PR. Protocol is in CLAUDE.md."],[171,"The Basis transcoder path is not exercised in CI (the KTX2 fixture is uncompressed RGBA8, since Node\nhas no Basis encoder); its files are built and served like Draco's."],[392,"The E2E global setup (`apps/web/e2e/global-setup.ts`) also renders the `make-capture.mjs` bike\nfrom each of its poses with `render-photos.mjs` (headless Chromium, three.js, the iPhone wide\ncamera's field of view) and writes `bike-photos.bikecapture.zip`, so photo close-ups are ranked\nand shown from real images of the fixture."],[332,"The iPhone app exports `*.bikecapture.zip` (format `bike-capture/1`, see\nArchitecture). To test the import path without a phone:"],[391,"The photos are PNG stand-ins: real captures have HEIC, which Node cannot encode."],[323,"The procedural demo bike loads with sample areas and comments."],[21,"The resulting scene gets a stable id (`capture-<name>-<createdAt digits>`) so dropping the same\nbundle again restores its saved areas and comments, and a model URL `bundle:<zip name>/<path>`,\nwhich is never fetched: it is resolved from memory or from the capture cache below, and only\nwhen neither has it does the viewer ask for that zip to be dropped again."],[155,"The script serves `dist/` with `vite preview`, drives Chromium on SwiftShader (like the E2E suite)\nthrough the `?e2e` test hook and prints JSON: boot time, a synchronous **frame cost** (render + a\n1-pixel readback that waits for the GPU), renders while idle and while orbiting with the mouse\n(with and without 50 pins), pin-update time per frame, and for `--model`: time until the first frame\nwith the model, geometry size, JS heap, frame cost and the cost of one `pick()` / `isOccluded()`."],[329,"The site is republished automatically on every push to the stack tip (the newest open PR nothing else is stacked on, or `develop` when none is open). Each open PR also gets its\nown copy at `https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (viewer at `/pr/<n>/app/`),\nlisted under **PR previews** on the home and Progress pages, so you can try a PR before\nmerging it. The home page says which commit and branch it was built from."],[416,"The viewer renders on demand: to wait for a picture to settle use `viewer.rendering === false`; `viewer.renderCount` counts drawn frames."],[117,"Things an agent cannot do (hardware, accounts, decisions). Newest first."],[359,"Three layers, cheapest first. CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs all of them on every PR."],[365,"three.js code that needs no WebGL (loaders, `centerOnGround`, the demo bike's geometry) is\ntested in Node too (`viewer-node.test.ts`). three's `FileLoader` needs a `ProgressEvent`\nstub in Node; the test file installs one. Models are passed as `data:` URLs."],[30,"three.js r186 can read this: `USDLoader` (the old `USDZLoader` is a deprecated alias) has a crate\nparser with LZ4 + integer decoding (`usd/USDCParser.js`) and a composer that handles xforms,\nGeomSubsets, indexed/face-varying primvars, UsdPreviewSurface textures, `metersPerUnit` and Z-up.\nWe reuse those parsers and patch what fails on real-world files:"],[328,"To try a capture bundle without the iPhone app, download the synthetic one:\n**https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/samples/synthetic-bike.bikecapture.zip**,\nthen in the viewer tap **Open…** and pick it from Files. A red low-poly bike replaces the demo\nand the scene is named \"Synthetic test bike\"."],[247,"Top priority: any photo set or video of a bike (any camera) must become a `bike-capture/1` bundle the viewer opens. Research and recommendation: docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md."],[103,"UI changes verified in Chromium with screenshots, at desktop and phone sizes."],[349,"Unit tests"],[67,"Unreleased"],[46,"Up sign by votes: the centroid sits below mid-height (wheels), and the top band (handlebar) is\nwider across than the bottom band (two tyre contact patches)."],[369,"USD: `usdz.test.ts` loads the committed binary USDC fixtures (`apps/web/test/fixtures/`, made\nby `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py` with Pixar USD); `usd-units.test.ts` drives the crate\ndecoders and composer fast paths directly for encodings the fixtures do not contain."],[6,"USDZ loading (`apps/web/src/viewer/usd/`)"],[84,"USDZ robustness: Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC) loads with textures; fixes three.js r186 crate decoding of inline vectors/halves/negative ints, ~10× faster mesh build for large captures, lazy-loaded USD code, clear fallback to `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`. Synthetic fixture generator `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`. (#3)"],[403,"Use `collectErrors(page)` and assert it is empty where a flow should be clean."],[397,"wait for state instead of sleeping: `ready` (boot finished), a model in `viewer.modelRoot`,\n`viewer.flying` (camera animation running);"],[241,"Web viewer: three.js, orbit, fly-to areas, background modes (clear / chroma green / studio / dark)"],[73,"WebKit E2E: the iPhone specs also run in Playwright WebKit (Safari's engine) via `npm run e2e:webkit` (local, on a Mac; CI is a roadmap item). (#16)"],[167,"Weld cost: ~0.2 s for 3M vertices in Node on an idle core (unrolled position/normal/uv path), BVH\nbuild ~1 s, now in a worker. Real-device numbers are still to be taken (see Known gaps)."],[320,"What each PR adds"],[350,"What is not unit-tested, and why"],[358,"What the suite covers"],[136,"What the viewer does"],[176,"Why bikes are hard"],[2,"Why Object Capture instead of Wes Bos' room pipeline"],[334,"With a real capture: AirDrop the `.bikecapture.zip` from the iPhone to the laptop and drop it on\nthe viewer. If the model does not show, note what the viewer says and add it to\nManual steps."],[357,"Writing reliable E2E tests"],[368,"Zip parsing: `zipIndex.test.ts` hand-builds zips byte by byte (zip64 records and extra fields,\nforeign extras, odd methods, lying sizes), branches fflate never writes."]],"type":"string"},"page_id":{"docs":{"1":7,"2":8,"3":9,"4":10,"5":11,"6":12,"7":13,"8":14,"9":15,"10":16,"11":17,"12":18,"13":19,"14":20,"15":21,"16":22,"17":23,"18":24,"19":25,"20":26,"21":27,"22":28,"23":29,"24":30,